 to score over 600 goals and is one of 34 players to record 1,300 points in his career . He is a past winner of the Mark Messier Leadership Award and has been recognized by both the Flames and the league for his community work ; while a member of the Flames , Iginla donated $ 2,000 to the children 's charity Kidsport for every goal he scored . His number 12 was retired by the Flames during a pre-game ceremony on March 2 , 2019 . Internationally , Iginla has represented Canada on numerous occasions .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "passage:/wiki/Jarome_Iginla", "traversal_to": "Jarome Iginla", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:0", "head": "Jarome Iginla", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:1996 World Junior Ice Hockey Championships:row:0", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "1996 World Junior Ice Hockey Championships", "row_index": 0, "column_name": "Player", "header_path": ["Player"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "Jarome Iginla", "traversal_to": "table:1996 World Junior Ice Hockey Championships:row:0", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:6", "head": "table:1996 World Junior Ice Hockey Championships:row:0", "relation": "gp", "tail": "table:1996 World Junior Ice Hockey Championships:row:0:cell:GP", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "1996 World Junior Ice Hockey Championships", "row_index": 0, "column_name": "GP", "header_path": ["GP"], "structural": true, "cell_node": true, "cell_value": "6", "traversal_from": "table:1996 World Junior Ice Hockey Championships:row:0", "traversal_to": "table:1996 World Junior Ice Hockey Championships:row:0:cell:GP", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Jarome Iginla --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Jarome_Iginla [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "Jarome Iginla --has_record--> table:1996 World Junior Ice Hockey Championships:row:0", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "table:1996 World Junior Ice Hockey Championships:row:0 --gp--> tabl