{"id": "de5b115416810d4b", "question": "What rice is a city famous for that has a sport where it is a non-lethal bloodsport ?", "gold_answer": "koshihikari", "answer": "koshihikari rice", "method": "path_text_top_n", "provider": "openai_compatible", "model": "GPT-OSS-120B", "temperature": 0.0, "latency_ms": 76246.13, "prompt_chars": 14716, "synthesis_prompt_chars": 14716, "grounding_prompt_chars": 0, "synthesis_retry_attempted": false, "raw_synthesis_response": "koshihikari rice", "request_max_output_tokens": 1024, "answer_retry_attempted": false, "answer_fallback_used": false, "retry_prompt_chars": 0, "raw_final_judge_response": null, "retry_raw_final_judge_response": null, "llm_selected_path_ids": ["row_5_30", "grounded_76", "grounded_83", "row_4_22", "answer_evidence_record_205", "answer_evidence_record_267", "answer_evidence_record_268"], "llm_selected_path_id": "row_5_30", "final_judge_evidence_edge_ids": ["record:210", "record:275", "record:211", "record:204", "record:205", "record:267", "record:268"], "final_judge_response_format": "deterministic_reverse_grounding", "final_judge_valid": true, "final_judge_failure_reason": null, "grounding_audit": {"status": "grounded", "mode": "deterministic_reverse_answer_match", "best_score": 83.0, "matched_edge_count": 7}, "kg_summary": {"num_nodes": 125, "num_edges": 137, "num_record_edges": 278, "num_text_contexts": 8, "num_contextualized_nodes": 28, "num_contextualized_edges": 32, "relations": ["date", "linked_passage", "location", "population", "remarks"], "num_rule_text_edges": 0, "num_entity_aliases": 4, "entity_resolution": {"lexical": 4}, "num_rejected_triples": 0, "num_extraction_errors": 0, "node_types": {"Kariwano tug of war ( 刈和野の大綱引き , Kariwano no ōtsuna-hiki )": ["Entity"], "15th day of 1st month": ["Attribute"], "Tug of war between two parts of Kariwano town featuring a giant straw rope , 80 cm ( 31 in ) diameter and over 200 m ( 660 ft ) long , held to pray for a rich harvest": ["Attribute"], "Daisen , Akita": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Sōma Wild horse racing ( 相馬野馬追 , Sōma Nomaoi )": ["Entity"], "Last Sat. , Sun . and Mon . of July": ["Attribute"], "Horseriding festival with riders clad in samurai armour of the Sengoku period , organized by Ōta Shrine , Odaka Shrine ( Minamisōma ) and Sōma Nakamura Shrine ( Sōma )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Sōma and Minamisōma Fukushima": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Dragon spirit festival of Chichibu Yoshida ( 秩父吉田の龍勢 , chichibu yoshida no ryūsei )": ["Entity"], "Second Sunday in October": ["Attribute"], "Shooting of homemade rockets from a scaffold structure , which when fired are meant to resemble dragons ascending to the heavens . The even is performed as appreciation for bountiful harvest": ["Attribute"], "Shimoyoshida , Chichibu , Saitama": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Hadaka Festival of Uchisa Bishomon Hall ( 浦佐毘沙門堂の裸押合 , uchisa bishamondō no hadaka oshiai )": ["Entity"], "March 3": ["Attribute"], "Naked festival of men struggling for rice cakes , sake and other auspicious objects . The event is seen as a prayer for safety and abundant crops but also constitutes rite of passage to adulthood": ["Attribute"], "Fukō-ji , Uchisa , Minamiuonuma , Niigata": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Bull wrestling ( 牛の角突きの習俗 , Ushi no tsunotsuki no shūzoku )": ["Entity"], "some time between May and November ( irregular )": ["Attribute"], "Ancient bull fighting event and only of its kind on Honshu": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Nagaoka , Ojiya and Uonuma , Niigata": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Tsuruga Nishimachi tug of war ( 敦賀西町の綱引き , Tsuruga Nishimachi no tsuna-hiki )": ["Entity"], "January 15": ["Attribute"], "Tug of war between two teams representing Daikoku and Ebisu . The year is said to bring a good harvest if Daikoku wins , and a good catch if Ebisu wins": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Tsuruga , Fukui": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Tajima Kutani tug of war ( 但馬久谷の菖蒲綱引き , Tajima Kutani shōbu tsuna-hiki )": ["Entity"], "June 5": ["Attribute"], "Tug of war between an adult and children group using a rope made of Japanese mugwort and sweet flag . If the adult group wins the 7th and final pull , it is said to become a good harvest . This is one of the five seasonal festivals ( gosekku )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Shin'onsen , Hyōgo": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Inaba tug of war ( 因幡の菖蒲綱引き , Inaba no shōbu tsuna-hiki )": ["Entity"], "5th day of 5th month closest weekend ( Aoya ) ; Sunday closest to the 5th day of the 5th month ( Mizushiri , Hōgi ) ; Sunday after June 5 ( Obaneo )": ["Attribute"], "Children tug of war with a rope made of sweet flag , Japanese mugwort and Japanese torreya . This is one of the five seasonal festivals ( gosekku )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Iwami and Tottori , Tottori": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Misasa tug of war ( 三朝のジンショ , Misasa no jinsho )": ["Entity"], "May 3 and 4": ["Attribute"], "Tug of war between the western and eastern parts of the district using a more than 80 m ( 260 ft ) , 4 t ( 3.9 long tons ; 4.4 short tons ) rope . A win of the east is said to be a good harvest , if the west wins business is going to prosper . This is one of the five seasonal festivals ( gosekku )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Misasa , Tottori": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Namari Momote Festival ( 生里のモモテ , namari no momote )": ["Entity"], "Sunday closest to 1st day of 2nd month": ["Attribute"], "Archery festival with origins in the early 10th century held in the precincts of Sanboko Shrine , in order to pray for an abundant harvest , bountiful fishing and to keep evil away": ["Attribute"], "Namari , Takuma , Mitoyo , Kagawa": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Yobuko tug of war ( 呼子の大綱引き , yobuko no ōtsunahiki )": ["Entity"], "first Saturday in June and the following Sunday": ["Attribute"], "Tug of war between a hill and beach team using a 400 m ( 1,300 ft ) long and 15 cm ( 5.9 in ) wide rope . If the beach team wins it is said to be bountiful fishing in this year , if the hill team wins , the year is said to produce abundant 