 known racetrack Mount Panorama is a landmark of the city . Bathurst has a historic city centre with many ornate buildings remaining from the gold rush period of the mid to late 19th century . The median age of the city 's population is 35 years ; which is particularly young for a regional centre ( the state median is 38 ) , and is related to the large education sector in the community . Population growth has reached 1.6% per annum over the five years until 2010 , making Bathurst the seventh fastest growing regional city in New South Wales . This growth over recent years has resulted in increased urban development including retail precincts , sporting facilities , housing estates and expanding industrial areas .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "passage:/wiki/Bathurst,_New_South_Wales", "traversal_to": "Bathurst, New South Wales", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:108", "head": "table:1884 New Zealand rugby union tour of New South Wales:row:5", "relation": "city", "tail": "Bathurst, New South Wales", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "1884 New Zealand rugby union tour of New South Wales", "row_index": 5, "column_name": "City", "header_path": ["City"], "structural": true, "derived_from_cell_split": true, "traversal_from": "Bathurst, New South Wales", "traversal_to": "table:1884 New Zealand rugby union tour of New South Wales:row:5", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:96", "head": "6", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:1884 New Zealand rugby union tour of New South Wales:row:5", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "1884 New Zealand rugby union tour of New South Wales", "row_index": 5, "column_name": "#", "header_path": ["#"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "table:1884 New Zealand rugby union tour of New South Wales:row:5", "traversal_to": "6", "direction": "reverse"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Bathurst, New South Wales --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Bathurst,_New_South_Wales [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": 