Chin . Benji ) : Chronicle of the Emperor Jing of Han Dynasty", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:528", "head": "Records of the Grand Historian ( 史記 , shiki , Chin . Shiji ) , vol . 11 of the Imperial Biographies ( 本紀 , Chin . Benji ) : Chronicle of the Emperor Jing of Han Dynasty", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Emperor_Jing_of_Han", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of National Treasures of Japan (writings: Chinese books)", "row_index": 2, "column_name": "Name", "header_path": ["Name"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Emperor_Jing_of_Han", "text": "Emperor Jing of Han ( 188 BC - 9 March 141 BC ) , personal name Liu Qi ( 劉啟 ) , was the sixth emperor of the Chinese Han dynasty from 157 to 141 BC . His reign saw the limiting of the power of the feudal kings/princes which resulted in the Rebellion of the Seven States in 154 BC . Emperor Jing managed to crush the revolt and princes were thereafter denied rights to appoint ministers for their fiefs . This move helped to consolidate central power which paved the way for the long reign of his son Emperor Wu of Han . Emperor Jing had a complicated personality . He continued his father Emperor Wen 's policy of general non-interference with the people , reduced tax and other burdens , and promoted government thrift . He continued and magnified his father 's policy of reduction in criminal sentences . His light governance of the people was due to the Taoist influences of his mother , Empress Dou . He was also criticized for general ungratefulness to others , including harsh treatments of Zhou Yafu , the general whose abilities allowed his victory in the Rebellion of the Seven States , and his wife Empress Bo . He was the last emperor of Han who was the common ancestor of all subsequent emperors ; all subsequent emperors of the Western Han were descendants of Emperor Wu , while all emperors of the Eastern Han were descendants of his sixth son Liu Fa , Prince Ding of Changsha .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "Records of the Grand Historian ( 史記 , shiki , Chin . Shiji ) , vol . 11 of the Imperial Biographies ( 本紀 , Chin . Benji ) : Chronicle of the Emperor Jing of Han Dynasty", "traversal_to": "passage:/wiki/Emperor_Jing_of_Han", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "table:List of National Treasures of Japan (writings: Chinese books):row:2 --present_location--> Tokyo Tokyo Daitokyu Memorial Library Daitōkyū Memorial Library ( 大東急記念文庫 , daitōkyū kinen bunko ) , Tokyo [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "Records of the Grand Historian ( 史記 , shiki , Chin . Shiji ) , vol . 11 of the Imperial Biographies ( 本紀 , Chin . Benji ) : Chronicle of the Emperor Jing of Han Dynasty --has_record--> table:List of National Treasures of Japan (writings: Chinese books):row:2 [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "Records of the Grand Historian ( 史記 , shiki , Chin . Shiji ) , vol . 11 of the Imperial Biographies ( 本紀 , Chin . Benji ) : Chronicle of the Emperor Jing of Han Dynasty --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Emperor_Jing_of_Han", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.7143, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 13.8833}}, {"path_id": "grounded_242", "score": 8.2333, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 2.0, "relation_match": 0.0, "text_context_match": 0.75, "query_coverage": 1.3333, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constraint_coverage": 0.0, "cross_modal_completeness": 1.5, "row_context": 0.0, "row_entity_binding": 0.0, "numeric_literal_coverage": 0.0, "strong_keyword_coverage": 0.0, "hyperlink_passage_bridge": 2.0, "table_witness_match": 0.0, "answer_type_path_filter": 0.0, "same_fact_corroboration": 0.0, "length_penalty": 0.35}, "nodes": ["Tokyo Tokyo Daitokyu Memorial 