German professional sports club based in Dortmund , North Rhine-Westphalia . It is best known for its men 's professional football team , which plays in the Bundesliga , the top tier of the German football league system . The club have won eight league championships , four DFB-Pokals , one UEFA Champions League , one Intercontinental Cup , and one UEFA Cup Winners ' Cup . Founded in 1909 by eighteen football players from Dortmund , the football team is part of a large membership-based sports club with more than 145,000 members , making Borussia Dortmund the second largest sports club by membership in Germany . Since 1974 , Dortmund have played their home games at Westfalenstadion ; the stadium is the largest in Germany , and Dortmund has the highest average attendance of any association football club in the world . Borussia Dortmund 's colours are black and yellow , giving the club its nickname die Schwarzgelben . The club has active departments in other sports , namely in women 's handball , and hold a long-standing rivalry with Ruhr neighbours Schalke 04 , known as the Revierderby . They also compete in Der Klassiker with fellow German club , Bayern Munich . In terms of Deloitte 's annual Football Money League , Dortmund was ranked as the second richest sports club in Germany , and the 12th richest football team in the world . Moreover , under the directorship of Michael Zorc in the 2010s , Dortmund have cultivated a reputation for spotting and developing young talent , and have remained focused on developing a youth system . They have also received plaudits for generally adhering to an attacking footballing philosophy .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "passage:/wiki/Borussia_Dortmund", "traversal_to": "Borussia Dortmund", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:69", "head": "table:List of English football transfers summer 2006:row:4", "relation": "moving_from", "tail": "Borussia Dortmund", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of English football transfers summer 2006", "row_index": 4, "column_name": "Moving from", "header_path": ["Moving from"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "Borussia Dortmund", "traversal_to": "table:List of English football transfers summer 2006:row:4", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:61", "head": "23 May 2006", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:List of English football transfers summer 2006:row:4", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of English football transfers summer 2006", "row_index": 4, "column_name": "Date", "header_path": ["Date"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "table:List of English football transfers summer 2006:row:4", "traversal_to": "23 May 2006", "direction": "reverse"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Borussia Dortmund --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Borussia_Dortmund [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "table:List of English football transfers summer 2006:row:4 --moving_from--> Borussia Dortmund [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "23 May 2006 --has_record--> table:List of English football transfers summer 2006:row:4 [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.625, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": false, "selection_score": 22.2091}}, {"path_id": "grounded_782", "score": 17.5727, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 1.5, "relation_match": 0.0, "text_context_match": 1.0, "query_coverage": 1.2727, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constraint_coverage": 0.0, "cross_modal_completeness": 1.5, "row_context": 1.0, "row_entity_binding": 1.0, "numeric_literal_coverage": 8.0, "strong_keyword_coverage": 0.0, "hyperlink_passage_bridge": 2.0, "table_witness_match": 0.0, "answer_type_path_filter": 0.0, "same_fact_corroboration": 0.0, "length_penalty": 0.7}, "nodes": ["23 May 2006", "table:List of English football transfers summer 2006:row:4", "Tomáš Rosický", "passage:/wiki/Tomáš_Rosický"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:61", "head": "23 May 2006", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:List of English football transfers summer 2006:row:4", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of English football transfers summer 2006", "row_index": 4, "column_name": "Date", "header_path": ["Date"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "23 May 2006", "traversal_to": "table:List of English football transfers summer 2006:row:4", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:66", "head": "table:List of English football transfers summer 2006:row:4", "relation": "name", "tail": "Tomáš Rosický", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of English football transfers summer 2006", "row_index": 4, "column_name": "Name", "header_path": ["Name"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "table:List of English football transfers summer 2006:row:4", "traversal_to": "Tomáš Rosický", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:319", "head": "Tomáš Rosický", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Tomáš_Rosický", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of English football transfers summer 2006", "row_index": 4, "column_name": "Name", "header_path": ["Name"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Tomáš_Rosický", "text": "Tomáš Rosický ( Czech pronunciation : [ ˈtomaːʃ ˈrosɪtskiː ] ; born 4 October 1980 ) is a Czech former professional footballer who was the captain of the Czech Republic national team for a ten-year period . He played club football for Sparta Prague , Borussia Dortmund and Arsenal . He was nicknamed the little Mozart for his ability to orchestrate the midfield . He started his professional career at his hometown club Sparta Prague , playing three seasons in the Czech First League before moving to Borussia Dortmund in 2001 for DM 25 million ( approximately £8 million ) , at the time a record transfer fee paid by a Bundesliga club . In his first season in Germany , he helped his team win the league title and reach the 2002 UEFA Cup Final . Rosický joined Arsenal in 2006 , and made 247 appearances for the club , including appearing in their victory in the 2014 FA Cup Final . He spent a total of ten seasons in the Premier League , affected by several long-term injuries . Internationally , Rosický made his debut for the Czech Republic in 2000 and became captain of his country in 2006 . He has taken part in four UEFA European Championships as well as the 2006 FIFA World Cup . He earned his 100th cap on 12 June 2015 . Rosický is the Czech Republic 's fourth highest goalscorer of all time .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "Tomáš Rosický", "traversal_to": "passage:/wiki/Tomáš_Rosický", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "23 May 2006 --has_record--> table:List of English football transfers summer 2006:row:4", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "table:List of English football transfers summer 2006:row:4 --name--> Tomáš Rosický", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "Tomáš Rosický --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Tomáš_Rosický", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.75, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 21.5727}}, {"path_id": "grounded_760", "score": 17.2091, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 2.0, "relation_match": 0.0, "text_context_match": 0.5, "query_coverage": 0.9091, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constraint_coverage": 0.0, "cross_modal_completeness": 1.5, "row_context": 1.0, "row_entity_binding": 1.0, "numeric_literal_coverage": 8.0, "strong_keyword_coverage": 0.0, "hyperlink_passage_bridge": 2.0, "table_witness_match": 0.0, "answer_type_path_filter": 0.0, "same_fact_corroboration": 0.0, "length_penalty": 0.7}, "nodes": ["23 May 2006", "table:List of English footbal