 country . Following an unsuccessful congressional bid in 2012 , McSally was first elected to the U.S. House of Representatives in 2014 . She served two terms as the U.S. Representative for Arizona 's 2nd congressional district . McSally was the Republican nominee in Arizona 's 2018 U.S. Senate election , losing 50-48% to Democratic Congresswoman Kyrsten Sinema , while Democrat Ann Kirkpatrick won McSally 's seat in the House elections . Following that election , interim U.S . Senator Jon Kyl announced his resignation from the state 's other Senate seat , and Republican Governor Doug Ducey appointed McSally to succeed Kyl . There will be a special election coinciding with the 2020 general election to determine whether McSally will serve the remainder of the Class 3 senate term , likely pitting her against astronaut and political activist Mark Kelly .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "Martha McSally", "traversal_to": "/wiki/Martha_McSally", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Martha McSally --notability--> Appointed to serve out remaining two years of late GOP Sen. John McCain 's term by Gov . Doug Ducey ( 2018- ) . Martha McSally is first U.S. Air Force Academy graduate to be appointed to U.S Senate ; pilot ; Retired as a Colonel ( United States ) in May 2010 after serving 22 years as a Fairchild Republic A-10 Thunderbolt II pilot [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "Martha McSally --linked_passage--> /wiki/Martha_McSally", "depends_on": 1}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.8235, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": false, "selection_score": 19.4833}}, {"path_id": "grounded_416", "score": 14.4833, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 1.5, "relation_match": 0.0, "text_context_match": 1.0, "query_coverage": 1.3333, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constr