ympics", "row_index": 6, "column_name": "Venue", "header_path": ["Venue"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Olympic_Sports_Centre_(Beijing)", "text": "The Olympic Sports Center Stadium ( simplified Chinese : 奥体中心体育场 ; traditional Chinese : 奧體中心體育場 ; pinyin : Ào Tǐ Zhōngxīn Tǐyùchǎng ) is a multi-purpose stadium in Beijing , China . It is currently used mostly for football matches . It was constructed in 1986 for the 1990 Asian Games . The complex contains the main stadium , an indoor arena , a hockey field , and a natatorium . It was renovated to host the 2008 Summer Olympics , where it hosted football matches and the running and riding parts of the modern pentathlon events . For the riding discipline , the football field at the core of the venue has been turned into a high-standard temporary equestrian field . The renovation also added four pavilion-styled rotating rampways around the stadium . The stadium has a floor space of 34,975 square meters , which exceeds the original building area of 20,000 square meters . Its capacity has doubled after the renovation , from about 18,000 to 36,228 .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "passage:/wiki/Olympic_Sports_Centre_(Beijing)", "traversal_to": "Olympic Sports Centre", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:57", "head": "Olympic Sports Centre", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:Venues of the 2008 Summer Olympics:row:6", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Venues of the 2008 Summer Olympics", "row_index": 6, "column_name": "Venue", "header_path": ["Venue"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "Olympic Sports Centre", "traversal_to": "table:Venues of the 2008 Summer Olympics:row:6", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:64", "head": "table:Venues of the 2008 Summer Olympics:row:6", "relation": "capacity", "tail": "table:Venues of the 2008 Summer Olympics:row:6:cell:Capacity", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Venues of the 2008 Summer Olympics", "row_index": 6, "column_name": "Capacity", "header_path": ["Capacity"], "structural": true, "cell_node": true, "cell_value": "36,228", "traversal_from": "table:Venues of the 2008 Summer Olympics:row:6", "traversal_to": "table:Venues of the 2008 Summer Olympics:row:6:cell:Capacity", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Olympic Sports Centre --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Olympic_Sports_Centre_(Beijing) [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "Olympic Sports Centre --has_record--> table:Venues of the 2008 Summer Olympics:row:6", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "table:Venues of the 2008 Summer Olympics:row:6 --capacity--> table:Venues of the 2008 Summer Olympics:row:6:cell:Capacity", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.6154, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 14.4111}}, {"path_id": "answer_evidence_record_113", "score": 83.0, "score_components": {"reverse_answer_match": 83.0}, "nodes": ["Capital Indoor Stadium", "passage:/wiki/Capital_Indoor_Stadium"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:113", "head": "Capital Indoor Stadium", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Capital_Indoor_Stadium", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Venues of the 2008 Summer Olympics", "row_index": 3, "column_name": "Venue", "header_path": ["Venue"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Capital_Indoor_Stadium", "text": "The Capital Indoor Stadium ( simplified Chinese : 首都体育馆 ; traditional Chinese : 首都體育館 ; pinyin : Shǒudū Tǐyùguǎn ) is an indoor arena in 56 Zhongguancun South Street , Beijing , China that was built in 1968 . It hosted matches between national table tennis teams of China and the United States in 1971 ; these matches were part of the exchange program known as ping pong diplomacy . It has a capacity of 17,345 and a floor space of 54,707 square meters expanded from the old 53,000 . It was renovated in 2001 to become a venue for the 2001 Summer Universiade . The stadium hosted one of the first NBA games in China , hosted on October 17 , 2004 in front of a sellout capacity of 17,903 . It also hosted the first-ever professional football game featuring all-stars from the Arena Football League to help promote the new AFL China league ( now known as the China Arena Football League . Capital Indoor Stadium has undergone a new renovation and expansion that was completed in late 2007 for the 2008 Summer Olympics , where it hosted volleyball tournaments . The venue is also used for figure skating , curling and ice hockey , which will also be used for the 2022 Winter Olympics .", "context_before": ""}]}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Capital Indoor Stadium --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Capital_Indoor_Stadium", "depends_on": null}], "path_verification": {"status": "answer_evidence", "selection_score": 83.0, "hard_failures": []}, "created_after_answer": true}, {"path_id": "answer_evidence_record_114", "score": 83.0, "score_components": {"reverse_answer_match": 83.0}, "nodes": ["Fengtai Softball Field", "passage:/wiki/Fengtai_Softball_Field"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:114", "head": "Fengtai Softball Field", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Fengtai_Softball_Field", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Venues of the 2008 Summer Olympics", "row_index": 4, "column_name": "Venue", "header_path": ["Venue"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Fengtai_Softball_Field", "text": "Fengtai Softball Field , or Fengtai Sports Center Softball Field ( simplified Chinese : 丰台体育中心垒球场 ; traditional Chinese : 豐臺體育中心壘球場 ; pinyin : Fēngtái Tǐyù Zhōngxīn Lěiqiúchǎng ) , is a softball stadium located in Beijing , China . It hosted the softball competitions at the 2008 Summer Olympics . The complex consists of two competition grounds and one training ground . The stadium has a capacity of 13,000 and a floor space of 15,570 square metres . It also has a backup field with a capacity of 3,500 and two training fields . It was also one of the venues of the 1990 Asian Games and the 1992 Women 's Softball World Cup Championships . The stadium 's renovation was completed on July 28 , 2006 , ready for the XI ISF Women 's World Championship in late August . It was the first Olympic venue in Beijing to be completed and put to use .", "context_before": "The Beijing Shooting Range Clay Target Field ( simplified Chinese : 北京射击场飞碟靶场 ; traditional Chinese : 北京射擊場飛碟靶場 ; pinyin : Běijīng Shèjīchǎng Fēidié Bǎchǎng ) is a shooting range in the Shijingshan District of Beijing , China . During the 1990 Asian Games , the shooting range was used for shooting and archery competitions . It was under renovation and was completed in August 2007 for the 2008 Summer Olympics . At the 2008 Olympics , the shooting range hosted men 's and women 's skeet shooting and trap shooting events . It has floor space of 6,170 square metres with a capacity of 5,000 seats which was reduced to 1,047 after the Games . The Capital Indoor Stadium ( simplified Chinese : 首都体育馆 ; traditional Chinese : 首都體育館 ; pinyin : Shǒudū Tǐyùguǎn ) is an indoor arena in 56 Zhongguancun South Street , Beijing , China that was built in 1968 . It hosted matches between national table tennis teams of China and the United States in 1971 ; these matches were part of the exchange program known as ping pong diplomacy . It has a capacity of 17,345 and a floor space of 54,707 square meters expanded from the old 53,000 . It was renovated in 2001 to become a venue for the 2001 Summer Universiade . The stadium hosted one of the first NBA games in China , hosted on October 17 , 2004 in front of a sellout capacity of 17,903 . It also hosted the first-ever professional football game featuring all-stars from the Arena Football League to help promote the new AFL China league ( now known as the China Arena Football League . Capital Indoor Stadium has undergone a new renovation and expansion that was completed in late 2007 for the 2008 Summer Olympics , where it hosted volleyball tournaments . The venue is also used for figure skating , curling and ice hockey , which will also be used for the 2022 Winter Olympics ."}]}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Fengtai Softball Field --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Fengtai_Softball_Field", "depends_on": null}], "path_verification": {"status": "answer_evidence", "selection_score": 83.0, "hard_failures": []}, "created_after_answer": true}, {"path_id": "answer_evidence_semantic_13_0", "score": 83.0, "score_components": {"reverse_answer_match": 83.0}, "nodes": ["Capital Indoor Stadium", "/wiki/Capital_Indoor_Stadium"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "semantic:13:0", "head": "Capital Indoor Stadium", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "/wiki/Capital_Indoor_Stadium", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Venues of the 2008 Summer Olympics", "source_group": null, "row_index": 3, "column_name": "Venue", "header_path": ["Venue"], "structural": false, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Capital_Indoor_Stadium", "text": "The Capital Indoor Stadium ( simplified Chinese : 首都体育馆 ; traditional Chinese : 首都體育館 ; pinyin : Shǒudū Tǐyùguǎn ) is an indoor arena in 56 Zhongguancun South Street , Beijing , China that was built in 1968 . It hosted matches between national table tennis teams of China and the United States in 1971 ; these matches were part of the exchange program known as ping pong diplomacy . It has a capacity of 17,345 and a floor space of 54,707 square meters expanded from the old 53,000 . It was renovated in 2001 to become a venue for the 2001 Summer Universiade . The stadium hosted one of the first NBA games in China , hosted on October 17 , 2004 in front of a sellout capacity of 17,903 . It also hosted the first-ever professional football game featuring all-stars from the Arena Football League to help promote the new AFL China league ( now known as the China Arena Football League . Capital Indoor Stadium has undergone a new renovation and expansion that was completed in late 2007 for the 2008 Summer Olympics , where it hosted volleyball tournaments . The venue is also used for figure skating , curling and ice hockey , which will also be used for the 2022 Winter Olympics .", "context_before": ""}]}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Capital Indoor Stadium --linked_passage--> /wiki/Capital_Indoor_Stadium", "depends_on": null}], "path_verification": {"status": "answer_evidence", "selection_score": 83.0, "hard_failures": []}, "created_after_answer": true}], "best_path_id": "grounded_304", "best_path_score": 11.0778, "execution_mode": "path_text", "code_generated": false, "program_executed": false, "text_extraction_mode": "direct_context_no_llm", "path_context_policy": "planner_top_n_paths_only", "top_n_paths": 5, "llm_calls": 1, "llm_api_attempts": 1, "llm_successful_calls": 1, "llm_failed_calls": 0, "llm_prompt_chars": 10893, "llm_response_chars": 10, "llm_latency_ms": 64057.8, "wall_time_ms": 74685.82, "non_llm_time_ms": 10628.02, "input_tokens": null, "output_tokens": null, "exact_match": 0.0, "semantic_exact_match": 0.0, "f1": 0.5, "execution_exact_match": null, "retrieval_audit": {"gold_row_recall": 1.0, "gold_hyperlink_recall": 1.0, "gold_passage_recall": 0.0}, "error_category": "retrieval_miss", "is_ambiguous": null, "ambiguity_status": null}
