e as he graduates from high school and becomes a freelance photographer , while also struggling with his studies , his friendship with his childhood best friend Harry Osborn , his growing feelings for his former high school crush Mary Jane Watson , and his dual life as Spider-Man . After progress on the film stalled for nearly 25 years , it was licensed for a worldwide release by Columbia Pictures in 1999 after it acquired options from Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer on all previous scripts developed by Cannon Films , Carolco , and New Cannon . Exercising its option on just two elements from the multi-script acquisition ( a different screenplay was written by James Cameron , Ted Newsom , John Brancato , Barney Cohen , and Joseph Goldman ) , Sony hired Koepp to create a working screenplay ( credited as Cameron 's ) , and Koepp received sole credit in final billing . Directors Roland Emmerich , Ang Lee , Chris Columbus , Jan de Bont , M. Night Shyamalan , Tony Scott , and David Fincher were considered to direct the project before Raimi was hired as director in 2000 . The Koepp script was rewritten by Scott Rosenberg during pre-production and received a dialogue polish from Alvin Sargent during production . Filming took place in Los Angeles and New York City from January 8 to June 30 , 2001 . Sony Pictures Imageworks handled the film 's visual effects . Spider-Man premiered at the Mann Village Theater on April 29 , 2002 , and was released in the United States four days later on May 3 .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "Spider-Man", "traversal_to": "/wiki/Spider-Man_(2002_film)", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Spider-Man --position--> Music Editor [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "Spider-Man --linked_passage--> /wiki/Spider-Man_(2002_film)", "depends_on": 1}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.6818, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": false, "selection_score": 14.775}}, {"path_id": "grounded_183", "score": 9.425, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 1.0, "relation_match": 0.0, "text_context_match": 1.0, "query_coverage": 1.125, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constraint_coverage": 0.0, "cross_modal_completeness": 1.5, "row_context": 0.0, "row_entity_binding": 0.0, "numeric_literal_coverage": 0.0, "strong_keyword_coverage": 2.5, "hyperlink_passage_bridge": 2.0, "table_witness_match": 0.0, "answer_type_path_filter": 0.0, "same_fact_corroboration": 0.0, "length_penalty": 0.7}, "nodes": ["Music Editor", "table:Chris Innis:row:9", "Spider-Man", "/wiki/Spider-Man_(2002_film)"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:91", "head": "table:Chris Innis:row:9", "relation": "position", "tail": "Music Editor", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Chris Innis", "row_index": 9, "column_name": "Position", "header_path": ["Position"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "Music Editor", "traversal_to": "table:Chris Innis:row:9", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:86", "head": "Spider-Man", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:Chris Innis:row:9", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Chris Innis", "row_index": 9, "column_name": "Title", "header_path": ["Title"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "table:Chris Innis:row:9", "traversal_to": "Spider-Man", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "semantic:37:0", "head": "Spider-Man", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "/wiki/Spider-Man_(2002_film)", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Chris Innis", "source_group": null, "row_index": 9, "column_name": "Title", "header_path": ["Title"], "structural": false, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Spider-Man_(2002_film)", "text": "Spider-Man is a 2002 American superhero film based on the Marvel Comics character of the same name . Directed by Sam Raimi from a screenplay by David Koepp , it is the first installment in the Spider-Man trilogy , and stars Tobey Maguire as the title character , alongside Willem Dafoe , Kirsten Dunst , James Franco , Cliff Robertson , and Rosemary Harris . The film centers on an outcast teen genius named Peter Parker , who develops spider-like superhuman abilities after being bitten by a genetically-altered spider . After his foster father/uncle is murdered by an armed felon , something of which he felt partially responsible , a guilt-ridden Parker is later driven to use his new abilities for a nobler purpose , as the hero/vigilante Spider-Man , to atone for his uncle 's murder . The rest of the film focuses on Parker 's efforts to balance his personal life as he graduates from high school and becomes a freelance photographer , while also struggling with his studies , his friendship with his childhood best friend Harry Osborn , his growing feelings for his former high school crush Mary Jane Watson , and his dual life as Spider-Man . After progress on the film stalled for nearly 25 years , it was licensed for a worldwide release by Columbia Pictures in 1999 after it acquired options from Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer on all previous scripts developed by Cannon Films , Carolco , and New Cannon . Exercising its option on just two elements from the multi-script acquisition ( a different screenplay was written by James Cameron , Ted Newsom , John Brancato , Barney Cohen , and Joseph Goldman ) , Sony hired Koepp to create a working screenplay ( credited as Cameron 's ) , and Koepp received sole credit in final billing . Directors Roland Emmerich , Ang Lee , Chris Columbus , Jan de Bont , M. Night Shyamalan , Tony Scott , and David Fincher were considered to direct the project before Raimi was hired as director in 2000 . The Koepp script was rewritten by Scott Rosenberg during pre-production and received a dialogue polish from Alvin Sargent during production . Filming took place in Los Angeles and New York City from January 8 to June 30 , 2001 . Sony Pictures Imageworks handled the film 's visual effects . Spider-Man premiered at the Mann Village Theater on April 29 , 2002 , and was released in the United States four days later on May 3 .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "Spider-Man", "traversal_to": "/wiki/Spider-Man_(2002_film)", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "table:Chris Innis:row:9 --position--> Music Editor [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "Spider-Man --has_record--> table:Chris Innis:row:9 [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "Spider-Man --linked_passage--> /wiki/Spider-Man_(2002_film)", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.6818, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": false, "selection_score": 14.425}}, {"path_id": "grounded_246", "score": 9.775, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 1.0, "relation_match": 0.0, "text_context_match": 1.0, "query_coverage": 1.125, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constraint_coverage": 0.0, "cross_modal_completeness": 1.5, "row_context": 0.0, "row_entity_binding": 0.0, "numeric_literal_coverage": 0.0, "strong_keyword_coverage": 2.5, "hyperlink_passage_bridge": 2.0, "table_witness_match": 0.0, "answer_type_path_filter": 0.0, "same_fact_corroboration": 0.0, "length_penalty": 0.35}, "nodes": ["Music Editor", "Spider-Man", "passage:/wiki/Spider-Man_(2002_film)"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "semantic:35:0", "head": "Spider-Man", "relation": "position", "tail": "Music Editor", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Chris Innis", "source_group": null, "row_index": 9, "column_name": "Position", "header_path": ["Position"], "structural": false, "contexts": [], "traversal_from": "Music Editor", "traversal_to": "Spider-Man", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:183", "head": "Spider-Man", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Spider-Man_(2002_film)", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Chris Innis", "row_index": 9, "column_name": "Title", "header_path": ["Title"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Spider-Man_(2002_film)", "text": "Spider-Man is a 2002 American superhero film based on the Marvel Comics character of the same name . Directed by Sam Raimi from a screenplay by David Koepp , it is the first installment in the Spider-Man trilogy , and stars Tobey Maguire as the title character , alongside Willem Dafoe , Kirsten Dunst , James Franco , Cliff Robertson , and Rosemary Harris . The film centers on an outcast teen genius named Peter Parker , who develops spider-like superhuman abilities after being bitten by a genetically-altered spider . After his foster father/uncle is murdered by an armed felon , something of which he felt partially responsible , a guilt-ridden Parker is later driven to use his new abilities for a nobler purpose , as the hero/vigilante Spider-Man , to atone for his uncle 's murder . The rest of the film focuses on Parker 's efforts to balance his personal life as he graduates from high school and becomes a freelance photographer , while also struggling with his studies , his friendship with his childhood best friend Harry Osborn , his growing feelings for his former high school crush Mary Jane Watson , and his dual life as Spider-Man . After progress on the film stalled for nearly 25 years , it was licensed for a worldwide release by Columbia Pictures in 1999 after it acquired options from Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer on all previous scripts developed by Cannon Films , Carolco , and New Cannon . Exercising its option on just two elements from the multi-script acquisition ( a different screenplay was written by James Cameron , Ted Newsom , John Brancato , Barney Cohen , and Joseph Goldman ) , Sony hired Koepp to create a working screenplay ( credited as Cameron 's ) , and Koepp received sole credit in final billing . Directors Roland Emmerich , Ang Lee , Chris Columbus , Jan de Bont , M. Night Shyamalan , Tony Scott , and David Fincher were considered to direct the project before Raimi was hired as director in 2000 . The Koepp script was rewritten by Scott Rosenberg during pre-production and received a dialogue polish from Alvin Sargent during production . Filming took place in Los Angeles and New York City from January 8 to June 30 , 2001 . Sony Pictures Imageworks handled the film 's visual effects . Spider-Man premiered at the Mann Village Theater on April 29 , 2002 , and was released in the United States four days later on May 3 .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "Spider-Man", "traversal_to": "passage:/wiki/Spider-Man_(2002_film)", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Spider-Man --position--> Music Editor [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "Spider-Man --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Spider-Man_(2002_film)", "depends_on": 1}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.6818, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 13.775}}, {"path_id": "grounded_135", "score": 9.55, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 1.0, "relation_match": 0.0, "text_context_match": 0.0, "query_coverage": 0.25, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constraint_coverage": 0.0, "cross_modal_completeness": 1.5, "row_context": 1.0, "row_entity_binding": 1.0, "numeric_literal_coverage": 0.0, "strong_keyword_coverage": 2.5, "hyperlink_passage_bridge": 2.0, "table_witness_match": 0.0, "answer_type_path_filter": 0.0, "same_fact_corroboration": 0.0, "length_penalty": 0.7}, "nodes": ["Music Editor", "table:Chris Innis:row:8", "The Gift", "passage:/wiki/The_Gift_(2000_film)"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:81", "head": "table:Chris Innis:row:8", "relation": "position", "tail": "Music Editor", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Chris Innis", "row_index": 8, "column_name": "Position", "header_path": ["Position"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "Music Editor", "traversal_to": "table:Chris Innis:row:8", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:76", "head": "The Gift", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:Chris Innis:row:8", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Chris Innis", "row_index": 8, "column_name": "Title", "header_path": ["Title"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "table:Chris Innis:row:8", "traversal_to": "The Gift", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:180", "head": "The Gift", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/The_Gift_(2000_film)", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Chris Innis", "row_index": 8, "column_name": "Title", "header_path": ["Title"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/The_Gift_(2000_film)", "text": "The Gift is a 2000 American supernatural thriller film directed by Sam Raimi , written by Billy Bob Thornton and Tom Epperson , and based on the alleged psychic experiences of Thornton 's mother . The film centers on Annie ( Cate Blanchett ) becoming involved in a murder case as a result of acquiring knowledge about the crime through extrasensory perception . The cast also includes Keanu Reeves , Giovanni Ribisi , Hilary Swank , Katie Holmes , and Greg Kinnear .", "context_before": "Sir Ridley Scott ( born 30 November 1937 ) is an English filmmaker . Following his commercial breakthrough in 1979 with the science fiction horror film Alien , further works include the neo-noir dystopian film Blade Runner , the road adventure film Thelma & Louise , the historical drama Gladiator ( which won the Academy Award for Best Picture ) and the science fiction film The Martian . Beginning his career in advertising where he honed his filmmaking skills by making inventive mini-films for television commercials , Scott 's work is known for its atmospheric , highly concentrated visual style . Though his films range widely in setting and period , they frequently showcase memorable imagery of urban environments , whether 2nd-century Rome ( Gladiator ) , 12th-century Jerusalem ( Kingdom of Heaven ) , Medieval England ( Robin Hood ) , contemporary Mogadishu ( Black Hawk Down ) , the future cityscapes of Blade Runner , or the distant planets in Alien , Prometheus , The Martian and Alien : Covenant . Several of his films are also known for their strong female characters . Scott has been nominated for three Academy Awards for Directing ( for Thelma & Louise , Gladiator and Black Hawk Down ) . In 1995 , both Ridley and his brother Tony received a BAFTA for Outstanding British Contribution To Cinema . In 2003 , Scott was knighted for his services to the British film industry . In a 2004 BBC poll , Scott was named the tenth most influential person in British culture . In 2015 , he received an honorary doctorate from the Royal College of Art in London , and in 2018 received the BAFTA Fellowship for lifetime achievement . Jeff Burr ( born 1963 , in Aurora , Ohio ) is an American film director , writer , and producer best known for his work in horror sequels , such as Stepfather II , The Texas Chainsaw Massacre III , Puppet Master 4 and 5 , and Pumpkinhead II ."}], "traversal_from": "The Gift", "traversal_to": "passage:/wiki/The_Gift_(2000_film)", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "table:Chris Innis:row:8 --position--> Music Editor [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "The Gift --has_record--> table:Chris Innis:row:8 [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "The Gift --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/The_Gift_(2000_film)", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.3636, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 13.55}}, {"path_id": "answer_evidence_record_88", "score": 100.5, "score_components": {"reverse_answer_match": 100.5}, "nodes": ["table:Chris Innis:row:9:cell:Title", "Spider-Man"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:88", "head": "table:Chris Innis:row:9:cell:Title", "relation": "cell_value", "tail": "Spider-Man", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Chris Innis", "row_index": 9, "column_name": "Title", "header_path": ["Title"], "structural": true, "cell_node": true}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "table:Chris Innis:row:9:cell:Title --cell_value--> Spider-Man", "depends_on": null}], "path_verification": {"status": "answer_evidence", "selection_score": 100.5, "hard_failures": []}, "created_after_answer": true}, {"path_id": "answer_evidence_semantic_36_0", "score": 100.0, "score_components": {"reverse_answer_match": 100.0}, "nodes": ["Spider-Man", "Director Sam Raimi"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "semantic:36:0", "head": "Spider-Man", "relation": "other_personnel", "tail": "Director Sam Raimi", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Chris Innis", "source_group": null, "row_index": 9, "column_name": "Other Personnel", "header_path": ["Other Personnel"], "structural": false, "contexts": []}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Spider-Man --other_personnel--> Director Sam Raimi", "depends_on": null}], "path_verification": {"status": "answer_evidence", "selection_score": 100.0, "hard_failures": []}, "created_after_answer": true}, {"path_id": "answer_evidence_record_169", "score": 83.0, "score_components": {"reverse_answer_match": 83.0}, "nodes": ["American Gothic", "passage:/wiki/American_Gothic_(1995_TV_series)"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:169", "head": "American Gothic", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/American_Gothic_(1995_TV_series)", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Chris Innis", "row_index": 4, "column_name": "Title", "header_path": ["Title"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/American_Gothic_(1995_TV_series)", "text": "American Gothic is an American horror series created by Shaun Cassidy and executive producer Sam Raimi . The show first aired on CBS on September 22 , 1995 , and was canceled after a single season on July 11 , 1996 .", "context_before": "The Quick and the Dead is a 1995 American Revisionist Western film directed by Sam Raimi , and starring Sharon Stone , Gene Hackman , Russell Crowe and Leonardo DiCaprio . The screenplay was written by Simon Moore but includes contributions from Joss Whedon . The story focuses on The Lady ( Stone ) , a gunfighter who rides into the frontier town of Redemption , controlled by John Herod ( Hackman ) . The Lady joins a deadly dueling competition in an attempt to exact revenge for her father 's death . Simon Moore 's script was purchased by Sony Pictures Entertainment in May 1993 , and actress Sharon Stone signed on as both star and co-producer . Development was fast tracked after director Sam Raimi 's hiring , and principal photography began in Old Tucson Studios in Arizona on November 21 , 1993 . The film was distributed by TriStar Pictures and was released in the US on February 10 , 1995 , to a dismal box office performance , receiving mixed reviews from critics . In later years , however , the film has earned critical praise especially for the performances , direction , cinematography and musical score , with some critics noting it as underrated in Raimi 's catalog . This was Russell Crowe 's American film debut and was Woody Strode 's final performance ( the film is dedicated to him ) , as well as the last theatrical release of Roberts Blossom who died in 2011 . The phrase the quick and the dead is from the Second Epistle to Timothy ( 2 Timothy 4:1 ) in various Bible versions , including the King James Bible , describing the final judgment . The plot of this film bears no resemblance to that of the 1987 film of the same name , which was based on a western novel by Louis L'Amour . Samuel M. Raimi ( born October 23 , 1959 ) is an American filmmaker , actor , and producer , primarily known for creating the cult horror Evil Dead series , and directing the Spider-Man trilogy ( 2002-2007 ) . He also directed the 1990 superhero film Darkman , the 1998 neo-noir crime-thriller A Simple Plan , the 2000 supernatural thriller film The Gift , the 2009 supernatural horror film Drag Me to Hell , and the 2013 Disney fantasy film Oz the Great and Powerful . Raimi has also produced several successful television series , including Hercules : The Legendary Journeys and its spin-off Xena : Warrior Princess . He founded the production company Renaissance Pictures in 1979 ."}]}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "American Gothic --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/American_Gothic_(1995_TV_series)", "depends_on": null}], "path_verification": {"status": "answer_evidence", "selection_score": 83.0, "hard_failures": []}, "created_after_answer": true}], "best_path_id": "grounded_182", "best_path_score": 11.425, "execution_mode": "path_text", "code_generated": false, "program_executed": false, "text_extraction_mode": "direct_context_no_llm", "path_context_policy": "planner_top_n_paths_only", "top_n_paths": 5, "llm_calls": 1, "llm_api_attempts": 1, "llm_successful_calls": 1, "llm_failed_calls": 0, "llm_prompt_chars": 9120, "llm_response_chars": 10, "llm_latency_ms": 47367.22, "wall_time_ms": 63123.68, "non_llm_time_ms": 15756.46, "input_tokens": null, "output_tokens": null, "exact_match": 1.0, "semantic_exact_match": 1.0, "f1": 1.0, "execution_exact_match": null, "retrieval_audit": {"gold_row_recall": 1.0, "gold_hyperlink_recall": 1.0, "gold_passage_recall": 0.0}, "error_category": null, "is_ambiguous": null, "ambiguity_status": null}
