on Sony Entertainment Television ( India ) which premiered on 27 June 2005 . The program was produced by the same production house of Indian Idol . The concept of the show was to select a pair of India 's best singers/performers . It is based on the Spanish Operación Triunfo and international Star Academy format of Endemol , better known in English under the UK title Fame Academy ; in Indian terms , it was essentially a mixture of Indian Idol and Big Brother TV shows . Fame Gurukul started out with 16 contestants living in a musical performance academy ( Gurukul ) . Every week ( normally ) one contestant was voted out of the show , and so on until two will remained in the end .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "passage:/wiki/Fame_Gurukul", "traversal_to": "Fame Gurukul", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:5", "head": "table:Indian Television Academy Awards:row:0", "relation": "show", "tail": "Fame Gurukul", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Indian Television Academy Awards", "row_index": 0, "column_name": "Show", "header_path": ["Show"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "Fame Gurukul", "traversal_to": "table:Indian Television Academy Awards:row:0", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:0", "head": "2005", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:Indian Television Academy Awards:row:0", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Indian Television Academy Awards", "row_index": 0, "column_name": "Year", "header_path": ["Year"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "table:Indian Television Academy Awards:row:0", "traversal_to": "2005", "direction": "reverse"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Fame Gurukul --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Fame_Gurukul [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "table:Indian Television Academy Awards:row:0 --show--> Fame Gurukul [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "2005 --has_record--> table:Indian Television Academy Awards:row:0 [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": 