 the country . It is the ninth-largest state in India , with an area of 135,192 km2 ( 52,198 sq mi ) . With a 2011 population of 25.5 million , Chhattisgarh is the 16th-most populated state in the country . A resource-rich state , it is a source of electricity and steel for the country , accounting for 15% of the total steel produced as well as large contributor of coal . Chhattisgarh is one of the fastest-developing states in India . The state was formed on 1 November 2000 by partitioning ten Chhattisgarhi and six Gondi-speaking southeastern districts of Madhya Pradesh . The capital city is Raipur . Chhattisgarh borders the states of Madhya Pradesh in the northwest , Uttar Pradesh in the north , Jharkhand in northeast , Maharashtra in the southwest , Telangana and Andhra Pradesh in the south , and Odisha in the southeast . Currently the state comprises 30 districts . The Gross State Domestic Product ( GSDP ) of Chhattisgarh is ₹3.63 lakh crore ( US $ 51 billion ) and the per capita GSDP ₹102,762 ( US $ 1,400 )", "context_before": "Dalli-Rajhara is a town and a municipality in Balod district in the state of Chhattisgarh , India . Dalli Rajhara is home of iron ore captive mines for Bhilai Steel Plant , the largest integrated steel plant in India . Dalli mines deposit was discovered by Pramatha Nath Bose , the first Indian graded officer of the Geological Survey of India around 1900 ."}], "traversal_from": "Chhattisgarh", "traversal_to": "passage:/wiki/Chhattisgarh", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Dhamtari --has_record--> table:List of towns in India by population:row:4", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "table:List of towns in India by population:row:4 --state--> Chhattisgarh", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "Chhattisgarh --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Chhattisgarh", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.5, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": true, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 14.8667}}, {"path_id": "row_11_34", "score": 5.2667, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 0.0, "relation_match": 0.6667, "text_context_match": 1.0, "query_coverage": 0.8, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constraint_coverage": 0.0, "cross_modal_completeness": 1.5, "row_context": 1.0, "row_entity_binding": 1.0, "numeric_literal_coverage": -3.0, "strong_keyword_coverage": 0.0, "hyperlink_passage_bridge": 2.0, "table_witness_match": 0.0, "answer_type_path_filter": 0.0, "same_fact_corroboration": 0.0, "length_penalty": 0.7}, "nodes": ["Dhuri", "table:List of towns in India by population:row:11", "Punjab", "passage:/wiki/Punjab,_India"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:132", "head": "Dhuri", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:List of towns in India by population:row:11", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of towns in India by population", "row_index": 11, "column_name": "Name of Town", "header_path": ["Name of Town"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "Dhuri", "traversal_to": "table:List of towns in India by population:row:11", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:137", "head": "table:List of towns in India by population:row:11", "relation": "state", "tail": "Punjab", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of towns in India by population", "row_index": 11, "column_name": "State", "header_path": ["State"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "table:List of towns in India by population:row:11", "traversal_to": "Punjab", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:266", "head": "Punjab", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Punjab,_India", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of towns in India by population", "row_index": 11, "column_name": "State", "header_path": ["State"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Punjab,_India", "text": "Punjab ( /pʌnˈdʒɑːb/ ( listen ) , Punjabi : [ pənˈdʒaːb ] ) is a state in northern India . Forming part of the larger Punjab region of the Indian subcontinent , the state is bordered by the Indian union territory of Jammu and Kashmir to the north , and the Indian states of Himachal Pradesh to the east , Haryana to the south and southeast , and Rajasthan to the southwest . It is bordered by the Pakistani province of Punjab to the west . The state covers an area of 50,362 square kilometres , 1.53% of India 's total geographical area . It is the 20th-largest Indian state by area . With 27,704,236 inhabitants at the 2011 census , Punjab is the 16th-largest state by population , comprising 22 districts . Punjabi is the most widely spoken and official language of the state . The main ethnic group are the Punjabis , with Sikhs ( 58% ) and Hindus ( 38% ) . The state capital is Chandigarh , a Union Territory and also the capital of the neighbouring state of Haryana . The five tributary rivers of the Indus River from which the region took its name are Sutlej , Ravi , Beas , Chenab and Jhelum Rivers ; Sutlej , Ravi and Beas are part of the Indian Punjab . The history of Punjab has witnessed the migration and settlement of innumerable races , forming a melting pot of Punjabi civilisation . The first traces of human habitation in India were found in the Punjab region .", "context_before": "Assam ( /ˈæsæm/ , Assamese : [ ɔxɔm ] ( listen ) ) is a state in northeastern India , situated south of the eastern Himalayas along the Brahmaputra and Barak River valleys . Assam covers an area of 78,438 km2 ( 30,285 sq mi ) . The state is bordered by Bhutan and Arunachal Pradesh to the north ; Nagaland and Manipur to the east ; Meghalaya , Tripura , Mizoram and Bangladesh to the south ; and West Bengal to the west via the Siliguri Corridor , a 22 kilometres ( 14 mi ) strip of land that connects the state to the rest of India . Assam is known for Assam tea and Assam silk . The state was the first site for oil drilling in Asia . Assam is home to the one-horned Indian rhinoceros , along with the wild water buffalo , pygmy hog , tiger and various species of Asiatic birds , and provides one of the last wild habitats for the Asian elephant . The Assamese economy is aided by wildlife tourism to Kaziranga National Park and Manas National Park , which are World Heritage Sites . Sal tree forests are found in the state which , as a result of abundant rainfall , look green all year round . Assam receives more rainfall than most parts of India ; this rain feeds the Brahmaputra River , whose tributaries and oxbow lakes provide the region with a hydro-geomorphic environment . Dhuri is a city in Sangrur District in the state of Punjab , India . The neighbouring towns of Dhuri are Sangrur , Malerkotla , Nabha , and Barnala ."}], "traversal_from": "Punjab", "traversal_to": "passage:/wiki/Punjab,_India", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Dhuri --has_record--> table:List of towns in India by population:row:11", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "table:List of towns in India by population:row:11 --state--> Punjab", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "Punjab --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Punjab,_India", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.5714, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": true, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 10.7667}}, {"path_id": "answer_evidence_record_248", "score": 163.0, "score_components": {"reverse_answer_match": 163.0}, "nodes": ["Devprayag", "passage:/wiki/Devprayag"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:248", "head": "Devprayag", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Devprayag", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of towns in India by population", "row_index": 3, "column_name": "Name of Town", "header_path": ["Name of Town"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Devprayag", "text": "Devprayag ( Deva prayāga ) is a town and a nagar panchayat ( municipality ) in Tehri Garhwal district in the state of Uttarakhand , India , and is one of the Panch Prayag ( five confluences ) of Alaknanda River where Alaknanda , Saraswati ( invisible as it is underground ) and Bhagirathi rivers meet and take the name Ganga .", "context_before": "Degana is a town municipality and headquarter to Sub-Division and Tehsil located in Nagaur district of Rajasthan , India . Degana Railway Junction was made at a small village in the pre-independence era on the Jaipur-Jodhpur railway track solely for the reason of having a railway-node for better operational control as there was a stretch of more than 300 km without any station in-between . With the passage of time , a Town came into being by drawing more and more dwellers and houses in last 50 years nearer to the railway station owing to better transport connectivity to more significant city centers like Jaipur , Jodhpur and Bikaner . The city now has headquarters for administrative units of the sub-division . Degana is 44 km From Makrana Railway station and 15 km from Gachhipura Railway station . Rajasthan ( /ˈrɑːdʒəstæn/ Hindustani pronunciation : [ raːdʒəsˈtʰaːn ] ( listen ) ; literally , Land of Kings ) is a state in northern India . The state covers an area of 342,239 square kilometres ( 132,139 sq mi ) or 10.4 percent of the total geographical area of India . It is the largest Indian state by area and the seventh largest by population . Rajasthan is located on the northwestern side of India , where it comprises most of the wide and inhospitable Thar Desert ( also known as the Great Indian Desert ) and shares a border with the Pakistani provinces of Punjab to the northwest and Sindh to the west , along the Sutlej-Indus river valley . Elsewhere it is bordered by five other Indian states : Punjab to the north ; Haryana and Uttar Pradesh to the northeast ; Madhya Pradesh to the southeast ; and Gujarat to the southwest . Major features include the ruins of the Indus Valley Civilisation at Kalibanga and Balathal , the Dilwara Temples , a Jain pilgrimage site at Rajasthan 's only hill station , Mount Abu , in the ancient Aravalli mountain range and in eastern Rajasthan , the Keoladeo National Park near Bharatpur , a World Heritage Site known for its bird life . Rajasthan is also home to three national tiger reserves , the Ranthambore National Park in Sawai Madhopur , Sariska Tiger Reserve in Alwar and Mukundra Hill Tiger Reserve in Kota . The state was formed on 30 March 1949 when Rajputana - the name adopted by the British Raj for its dependencies in the region - was merged into the Dominion of India . Its capital and largest city is Jaipur . Other important cities are Jodhpur , Kota , Bikaner , Ajmer and Udaipur . The economy of Rajasthan is the ninth-largest state economy in India with ₹9.24 lakh crore ( US $ 130 billion ) in gross domestic product and a per capita GDP of ₹108,000 ( US $ 1,500 ) . Rajasthan ranks 22nd among Indian states in human development index ."}]}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Devprayag --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Devprayag", "depends_on": null}], "path_verification": {"status": "answer_evidence", "selection_score": 163.0, "hard_failures": []}, "created_after_answer": true}, {"path_id": "answer_evidence_semantic_20_0", "score": 163.0, "score_components": {"reverse_answer_match": 163.0}, "nodes": ["Devprayag", "/wiki/Devprayag"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "semantic:20:0", "head": "Devprayag", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "/wiki/Devprayag", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of towns in India by population", "source_group": null, "row_index": 3, "column_name": "Name of Town", "header_path": ["Name of Town"], "structural": false, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Devprayag", "text": "Devprayag ( Deva prayāga ) is a town and a nagar panchayat ( municipality ) in Tehri Garhwal district in the state of Uttarakhand , India , and is one of the Panch Prayag ( five confluences ) of Alaknanda River where Alaknanda , Saraswati ( invisible as it is underground ) and Bhagirathi rivers meet and take the name Ganga .", "context_before": "Degana is a town municipality and headquarter to Sub-Division and Tehsil located in Nagaur district of Rajasthan , India . Degana Railway Junction was made at a small village in the pre-independence era on the Jaipur-Jodhpur railway track solely for the reason of having a railway-node for better operational control as there was a stretch of more than 300 km without any station in-between . With the passage of time , a Town came into being by drawing more and more dwellers and houses in last 50 years nearer to the railway station owing to better transport connectivity to more significant city centers like Jaipur , Jodhpur and Bikaner . The city now has headquarters for administrative units of the sub-division . Degana is 44 km From Makrana Railway station and 15 km from Gachhipura Railway station . Rajasthan ( /ˈrɑːdʒəstæn/ Hindustani pronunciation : [ raːdʒəsˈtʰaːn ] ( listen ) ; literally , Land of Kings ) is a state in northern India . The state covers an area of 342,239 square kilometres ( 132,139 sq mi ) or 10.4 percent of the total geographical area of India . It is the largest Indian state by area and the seventh largest by population . Rajasthan is located on the northwestern side of India , where it comprises most of the wide and inhospitable Thar Desert ( also known as the Great Indian Desert ) and shares a border with the Pakistani provinces of Punjab to the northwest and Sindh to the west , along the Sutlej-Indus river valley . Elsewhere it is bordered by five other Indian states : Punjab to the north ; Haryana and Uttar Pradesh to the northeast ; Madhya Pradesh to the southeast ; and Gujarat to the southwest . Major features include the ruins of the Indus Valley Civilisation at Kalibanga and Balathal , the Dilwara Temples , a Jain pilgrimage site at Rajasthan 's only hill station , Mount Abu , in the ancient Aravalli mountain range and in eastern Rajasthan , the Keoladeo National Park near Bharatpur , a World Heritage Site known for its bird life . Rajasthan is also home to three national tiger reserves , the Ranthambore National Park in Sawai Madhopur , Sariska Tiger Reserve in Alwar and Mukundra Hill Tiger Reserve in Kota . The state was formed on 30 March 1949 when Rajputana - the name adopted by the British Raj for its dependencies in the region - was merged into the Dominion of India . Its capital and largest city is Jaipur . Other important cities are Jodhpur , Kota , Bikaner , Ajmer and Udaipur . The economy of Rajasthan is the ninth-largest state economy in India with ₹9.24 lakh crore ( US $ 130 billion ) in gross domestic product and a per capita GDP of ₹108,000 ( US $ 1,500 ) . Rajasthan ranks 22nd among Indian states in human development index ."}]}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Devprayag --linked_passage--> /wiki/Devprayag", "depends_on": null}], "path_verification": {"status": "answer_evidence", "selection_score": 163.0, "hard_failures": []}, "created_after_answer": true}], "best_path_id": "row_bridge_0_2", "best_path_score": 10.0667, "execution_mode": "path_text", "code_generated": false, "program_executed": false, "text_extraction_mode": "direct_context_no_llm", "path_context_policy": "planner_top_n_paths_only", "top_n_paths": 5, "llm_calls": 1, "llm_api_attempts": 1, "llm_successful_calls": 1, "llm_failed_calls": 0, "llm_prompt_chars": 10885, "llm_response_chars": 4, "llm_latency_ms": 57625.72, "wall_time_ms": 72012.71, "non_llm_time_ms": 14386.99, "input_tokens": null, "output_tokens": null, "exact_match": 1.0, "semantic_exact_match": 1.0, "f1": 1.0, "execution_exact_match": null, "retrieval_audit": {"gold_row_recall": 1.0, "gold_hyperlink_recall": 1.0, "gold_passage_recall": 0.0}, "error_category": null, "is_ambiguous": null, "ambiguity_status": null}
{"id": "00c882d1bfbc8aa3", "question": "What is the description if the dish that is a localised version of Indian Achaar ?", "gold_answer": "Various chopped vegetables in vinegar", "answer": "Various chopped vegetables in vinegar", "method": "path_text_top_n", "provider": "openai_compatible", "model": "GPT-OSS-120B", "temperature": 0.0, "latency_ms": 59382.99, "prompt_chars": 11516, "synthesis_prompt_chars": 11516, "grounding_prompt_chars": 0, "synthesis_retry_attempted": false, "raw_synthesis_response": "Various chopped vegetables in vinegar", "request_max_output_tokens": 1024, "answer_retry_attempted": false, "answer_fallback_used": false, "retry_prompt_chars": 0, "raw_final_judge_response": null, "retry_raw_final_judge_response": null, "llm_selected_path_ids": ["grounded_431", "answer_evidence_record_10"], "llm_selected_path_id": "grounded_431", "final_judge_evidence_edge_ids": ["record:11", "record:10"], "final_judge_response_format": "deterministic_reverse_grounding", "final_judge_valid": true, "final_judge_failure_reason": null, "grounding_audit": {"status": "grounded", "mode": "deterministic_reverse_answer_match", "best_score": 101.0, "matched_edge_count": 2}, "kg_summary": {"num_nodes": 46, "num_edges": 48, "num_record_edges": 134, "num_text_contexts": 8, "num_contextualized_nodes": 9, "num_contextualized_edges": 10, "relations": ["description", "linked_passage", "region", "type"], "num_rule_text_edges": 0, "num_entity_aliases": 0, "entity_resolution": {}, "num_rejected_triples": 0, "num_extraction_errors": 0, "node_types": {"Acar": ["Entity"], "Nationwide": ["Attribute"], "Pickles": ["Attribute"], "Various chopped vegetables in vinegar": ["Attribute"], "Bawang goreng": ["Entity"], "Garnish": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Crispy fried onions or shallots sprinkled upon various dishes to give aroma and crispy texture": ["Attribute"], "Dabu-dabu": ["Entity"], "North Sulawesi": ["Attribute"], "Sauce": ["Attribute"], "Sliced chili , tomatoes and shallots . Condiments for grilled fish": ["Attribute"], "Kecap manis and kecap asin": ["Entity"], "Soy sauces , available in sweet ( manis ) and salty ( asin )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Pecel": ["Entity"], "Java": ["Attribute"], "A mixture of vegetables and a type of traditional cracker with spicy peanut paste . Madiun and blitar in East Java are popular for their pecel": ["Attribute"], "Sambal": ["Entity"], "Chili sauce with rich variants across Indonesia , among other uses shrimp paste": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Serundeng": ["Entity"], "Sprinkle dry condiments": ["Attribute"], "Grated coconut sauteed and spiced , can be served with beef , sprinkled on soto , or eaten with sticky rice": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Tauco": ["Entity"], "Tauco is a paste made from preserved fermented yellow soybeans": ["Attribute"], "Tumpang": ["Entity"], "Tumpang or sambal tumpang is a typical food from Kediri , East Java . Sambal tumpang has been made of rotten tempeh mixed and cooked with various spices such as chili , onion , salt and other spices": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "/wiki/Acar": ["Attribute"], "/wiki/Garnish_(food)": ["Attribute"], "/wiki/Dabu-dabu": ["Attribute"], "/wiki/Kecap_manis": ["Attribute"], "Kecap manis": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Kecap_asin": ["Attribute"], "Kecap asin": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Soy_sauce": ["Attribute"], "Soy sauce": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Pecel": ["Attribute"], "/wiki/Sambal": ["Attribute"], "/wiki/Shrimp_paste": ["Attribute"], "Shrimp paste": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Serundeng": ["Attribute"], "/wiki/Coconut": ["Attribute"], "Coconut": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Tauco": ["Attribute"], "/wiki/Kediri_(city)": ["Attribute"], "Kediri": ["Entity"], "/wiki/East_Java": ["Attribute"], "East Java": ["Entity"]}}, "entity_anchor": {"direct_mentions": ["Indian Achaar"], "entity_type": null, "target_attribute": null, "constraints": {}, "bridge_entities": [], "table_constraints": [], "table_witnesses": []}, "retrieval_trace": {"strategy": "two_stage_bm25_schema", "stage1_top_k": 5, "max_table_rows": null, "selected_table_rows": 9, "stage2_budget": 3, "expansion_queries": ["Name Region Type Description"], "table_constraints": [], "table_witnesses": [], "entity_anchor": {"direct_mentions": ["Indian Achaar"], "entity_type": null, "target_attribute": null, "constraints": {}, "bridge_entities": [], "table_constraints": [], "table_witnesses": []}, "selected_row_hyperlinks": ["/wiki/Acar", "/wiki/Garnish_(food)", "/wiki/Dabu-dabu", "/wiki/Kecap_manis", "/wiki/Kecap_asin", "/wiki/Soy_sauce", "/wiki/Pecel", "/wiki/Sambal", "/wiki/Shrimp_paste", "/wiki/Serundeng", "/wiki/Coconut", "/wiki/Tauco", "/wiki/Kediri_(city)", "/wiki/East_Java"], "use_hyperlink_expansion": true, "passage_reranker_query": "question_plus_selected_rows", "selected_table_row_indices": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], "constraint_policy": {"allowed_output_values": [], "require_table_evidence": false}}, "path_selection_audit": {"candidate_path_ids": ["grounded_226", "grounded_431", "grounded_225", "grounded_430", "grounded_1508"], "qualified_path_ids": ["grounded_226", "grounded_431", "grounded_225", "grounded_430", "grounded_1508"], "rejected_path_ids": [], "abstained_for_missing_grounding": false, "pre_answer_path_selection": false, "verification_by_path": {"grounded_226": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.9091, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": false, "selection_score": 13.9667}, "grounded_431": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.8182, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": false, "selection_score": 13.7167}, "grounded_225": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.9091, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 13.4667}, "grounded_430": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.8182, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 13.2167}, "grounded_1508": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.5455, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 12.2167}}}, "reasoning_paths": [{"path_id": "grounded_226", "score": 8.9667, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 0.0, "relation_match": 0.6667, "text_context_match": 1.0, "query_coverage": 1.5, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constraint_coverage": 0.0, "cross_modal_completeness": 1.5, "row_context": 1.0, "row_entity_binding": 1.0, "numeric_literal_coverage": 0.0, "strong_keyword_coverage": 0.0, "hyperlink_passage_bridge": 2.0, "table_witness_match": 0.0, "answer_type_path_filter": 0.0, "same_fact_corroboration": 0.0, "length_penalty": 0.7}, "nodes": ["passage:/wiki/Dabu-dabu", "Dabu-dabu", "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:2", "Sliced chili , tomatoes and shallots . Condiments for grilled fish"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:115", "head": "Dabu-dabu", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Dabu-dabu", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of Indonesian dishes", "row_index": 2, "column_name": "Name", "header_path": ["Name"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Dabu-dabu", "text": "Dabu-dabu is a type of hot and spicy condiment commonly found in Manado cuisine of North Sulawesi , Indonesia . Dabu-dabu chopped red chili peppers , bird 's eye chili , shallots , red and green tomatoes , and a pinch of salt and sugar . All of the chopped and diced spices are mixed with fresh calamansi juice or locally known as lemon cui or jeruk kesturi ; sometimes calamansi is replaced by kaffir lime or lemon juice . The chili pepper and citrus juice give it a fresh sour and spicy flavour . It is usually used as a condiment for seafoods , especially various recipes of ikan bakar ( grilled fish ) . Dabu-dabu has a flavor similar to Mexican salsa . It is sometimes described as Manado 's raw sambal .", "context_before": "Acar is a type of vegetable pickle from Indonesia , and popular in Malaysia , Singapore and Brunei . It is a localised version of Indian Achaar . It is known as atjar in Dutch cuisine , derived from Indonesian acar . Acar is usually prepared in bulk as it may easily be stored in a well-sealed glass jar in refrigerator for a week , and served as the condiment for any meals . Pickling originated in India in 2400 BCE , Indian achaar pickle transmitted to Philippines as atchara via acar of Indonesia , Malaysia , Singapore and Brunei . A garnish is an item or substance used as a decoration or embellishment accompanying a prepared food dish or drink . In many cases , it may give added or contrasting flavor . Some garnishes are selected mainly to augment the visual impact of the plate , while others are selected specifically for the flavor they may impart . This is in contrast to a condiment , a prepared sauce added to another food item primarily for its flavor . A food item which is served with garnish may be described as being garni , the French term for 'garnished ' . Many garnishes are not intended to be eaten , though for some it is fine to do so . Parsley is an example of a traditional garnish ; this pungent green herb has small distinctly shaped leaves , firm stems , and is easy to trim into a garnish ."}], "traversal_from": "passage:/wiki/Dabu-dabu", "traversal_to": "Dabu-dabu", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:24", "head": "Dabu-dabu", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:2", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of Indonesian dishes", "row_index": 2, "column_name": "Name", "header_path": ["Name"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "Dabu-dabu", "traversal_to": "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:2", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:35", "head": "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:2", "relation": "description", "tail": "Sliced chili , tomatoes and shallots . Condiments for grilled fish", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of Indonesian dishes", "row_index": 2, "column_name": "Description", "header_path": ["Description"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:2", "traversal_to": "Sliced chili , tomatoes and shallots . Condiments for grilled fish", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Dabu-dabu --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Dabu-dabu [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "Dabu-dabu --has_record--> table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:2", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:2 --description--> Sliced chili , tomatoes and shallots . Condiments for grilled fish", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.9091, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": false, "selection_score": 13.9667}}, {"path_id": "grounded_431", "score": 8.7167, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 0.0, "relation_match": 0.6667, "text_context_match": 1.0, "query_coverage": 1.25, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constraint_coverage": 0.0, "cross_modal_completeness": 1.5, "row_context": 1.0, "row_entity_binding": 1.0, "numeric_literal_coverage": 0.0, "strong_keyword_coverage": 0.0, "hyperlink_passage_bridge": 2.0, "table_witness_match": 0.0, "answer_type_path_filter": 0.0, "same_fact_corroboration": 0.0, "length_penalty": 0.7}, "nodes": ["passage:/wiki/Acar", "Acar", "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:0", "Various chopped vegetables in vinegar"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:113", "head": "Acar", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Acar", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of Indonesian dishes", "row_index": 0, "column_name": "Name", "header_path": ["Name"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Acar", "text": "Acar is a type of vegetable pickle from Indonesia , and popular in Malaysia , Singapore and Brunei . It is a localised version of Indian Achaar . It is known as atjar in Dutch cuisine , derived from Indonesian acar . Acar is usually prepared in bulk as it may easily be stored in a well-sealed glass jar in refrigerator for a week , and served as the condiment for any meals . Pickling originated in India in 2400 BCE , Indian achaar pickle transmitted to Philippines as atchara via acar of Indonesia , Malaysia , Singapore and Brunei .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "passage:/wiki/Acar", "traversal_to": "Acar", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:0", "head": "Acar", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:0", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of Indonesian dishes", "row_index": 0, "column_name": "Name", "header_path": ["Name"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "Acar", "traversal_to": "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:0", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:11", "head": "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:0", "relation": "description", "tail": "Various chopped vegetables in vinegar", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of Indonesian dishes", "row_index": 0, "column_name": "Description", "header_path": ["Description"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:0", "traversal_to": "Various chopped vegetables in vinegar", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Acar --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Acar [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "Acar --has_record--> table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:0", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:0 --description--> Various chopped vegetables in vinegar", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.8182, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": false, "selection_score": 13.7167}}, {"path_id": "grounded_225", "score": 9.4667, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 0.5, "relation_match": 0.6667, "text_context_match": 1.0, "query_coverage": 1.5, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constraint_coverage": 0.0, "cross_modal_completeness": 1.5, "row_context": 1.0, "row_entity_binding": 1.0, "numeric_literal_coverage": 0.0, "strong_keyword_coverage": 0.0, "hyperlink_passage_bridge": 2.0, "table_witness_match": 0.0, "answer_type_path_filter": 0.0, "same_fact_corroboration": 0.0, "length_penalty": 0.7}, "nodes": ["passage:/wiki/Dabu-dabu", "Dabu-dabu", "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:2", "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:2:cell:Description"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:115", "head": "Dabu-dabu", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Dabu-dabu", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of Indonesian dishes", "row_index": 2, "column_name": "Name", "header_path": ["Name"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Dabu-dabu", "text": "Dabu-dabu is a type of hot and spicy condiment commonly found in Manado cuisine of North Sulawesi , Indonesia . Dabu-dabu chopped red chili peppers , bird 's eye chili , shallots , red and green tomatoes , and a pinch of salt and sugar . All of the chopped and diced spices are mixed with fresh calamansi juice or locally known as lemon cui or jeruk kesturi ; sometimes calamansi is replaced by kaffir lime or lemon juice . The chili pepper and citrus juice give it a fresh sour and spicy flavour . It is usually used as a condiment for seafoods , especially various recipes of ikan bakar ( grilled fish ) . Dabu-dabu has a flavor similar to Mexican salsa . It is sometimes described as Manado 's raw sambal .", "context_before": "Acar is a type of vegetable pickle from Indonesia , and popular in Malaysia , Singapore and Brunei . It is a localised version of Indian Achaar . It is known as atjar in Dutch cuisine , derived from Indonesian acar . Acar is usually prepared in bulk as it may easily be stored in a well-sealed glass jar in refrigerator for a week , and served as the condiment for any meals . Pickling originated in India in 2400 BCE , Indian achaar pickle transmitted to Philippines as atchara via acar of Indonesia , Malaysia , Singapore and Brunei . A garnish is an item or substance used as a decoration or embellishment accompanying a prepared food dish or drink . In many cases , it may give added or contrasting flavor . Some garnishes are selected mainly to augment the visual impact of the plate , while others are selected specifically for the flavor they may impart . This is in contrast to a condiment , a prepared sauce added to another food item primarily for its flavor . A food item which is served with garnish may be described as being garni , the French term for 'garnished ' . Many garnishes are not intended to be eaten , though for some it is fine to do so . Parsley is an example of a traditional garnish ; this pungent green herb has small distinctly shaped leaves , firm stems , and is easy to trim into a garnish ."}], "traversal_from": "passage:/wiki/Dabu-dabu", "traversal_to": "Dabu-dabu", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:24", "head": "Dabu-dabu", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:2", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of Indonesian dishes", "row_index": 2, "column_name": "Name", "header_path": ["Name"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "Dabu-dabu", "traversal_to": "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:2", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:33", "head": "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:2", "relation": "description", "tail": "table:List of Indonesian dishes:row:2:cell:Description", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List 