e_Old_Arrow_Tree,_California", "text": "The Old Arrow Tree is California Historical Landmark Number 164 . For many years , people placed twigs , arrows or feathers into the bark of the tree as they passed . There are two suggestions of why there were so many arrows in the tree . One story says that the Indians respected this tall , straight redwood , calling it a great warrior and that shooting it was a form of respect . The other tale is that it marks war between the Hoopa and Korbel tribes . The Korbel won and afterwards Indians passing the tree would put an arrow into it , to show they arrived in peace . There is no official marker at this location .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "The Old Arrow Tree", "traversal_to": "/wiki/The_Old_Arrow_Tree,_California", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "The Old Arrow Tree --linked_passage--> /wiki/The_Old_Arrow_Tree,_California", "depends_on": null}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.5, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": false, "selection_score": 17.4167}}, {"path_id": "grounded_238", "score": 12.4167, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 1.5, "relation_match": 0.0, "text_context_match": 0.75, "query_coverage": 0.6667, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constraint_coverage": 0.0, "cross_modal_completeness": 1.5, "row_context": 0.0, "row_entity_binding": 0.0, "numeric_literal_coverage": 0.0, "strong_keyword_coverage": 5.0, "hyperlink_passage_bridge": 2.0, "table_witness_match": 0.0, "answer_type_path_filter": 0.0, "same_fact_corroboration": 0.0, "length_penalty": 0.0}, "nodes": ["/wiki/The_Old_Arrow_Tree,_California", "The Old Arrow Tree"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "semantic:47:0", "head": "The Old Arrow Tree", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "/wiki/The_Old_Arrow_Tree,_California", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "California Hi