z,_Mississippi", "text": "Natchez ( /ˈnætʃɪz/ ) is the county seat and only city of Adams County , Mississippi , United States . Natchez has a total population of 15,792 ( as of the 2010 census ) . Located on the Mississippi River across from Vidalia in Concordia Parish , Louisiana , Natchez was a prominent city in the antebellum years , a center of cotton planters and Mississippi River trade . Natchez is some 90 miles ( 140 km ) southwest of Jackson , the capital of Mississippi , which is located near the center of the state . It is approximately 85 miles ( 137 km ) north of Baton Rouge , Louisiana , located on the lower Mississippi River . Natchez is the 25th-largest city in the state . The city was named for the Natchez tribe of Native Americans , who with their ancestors , inhabited much of the area from the 8th century AD through the French colonial period .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "Natchez", "traversal_to": "passage:/wiki/Natchez,_Mississippi", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "5 --has_record--> table:National Register of Historic Places listings in Jefferson County, Mississippi:row:4", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "table:National Register of Historic Places listings in Jefferson County, Mississippi:row:4 --city_or_town--> Natchez", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "Natchez --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Natchez,_Mississippi", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.625, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 14.8333}}, {"path_id": "answer_evidence_record_418", "score": 163.0, "score_components": {"reverse_answer_match": 163.0}, "nodes": ["Fayette", "passage:/wiki/Fayette,_Mississippi"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:418", "head": "Fayette", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Fayette,_Mississippi", "source_type": "table