nd his work with pianist Lennie Tristano . He was notable during this era as one of relatively few alto saxophonists to retain a distinctive style when Charlie Parker exerted a massive influence . Like other students of Tristano , Konitz was noted for improvising long , melodic lines with the rhythmic interest coming from odd accents , or odd note groupings suggestive of the imposition of one time signature over another . Other saxophonists were strongly influenced by Konitz , notably Paul Desmond and Art Pepper .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "passage:/wiki/Lee_Konitz", "traversal_to": "With Lee Konitz ( alto sax ) , Zoot Sims ( tenor sax , alto sax ) , Al Cohn ( tenor sax , baritone sax ) , Freddie Green ( guitar ) , Henry Grimes ( bass ) , Dave Bailey ( drums )", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:155", "head": "table:Allen Eager:row:9", "relation": "notes", "tail": "With Lee Konitz ( alto sax ) , Zoot Sims ( tenor sax , alto sax ) , Al Cohn ( tenor sax , baritone sax ) , Freddie Green ( guitar ) , Henry Grimes ( bass ) , Dave Bailey ( drums )", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Allen Eager", "row_index": 9, "column_name": "Notes", "header_path": ["Notes"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "With Lee Konitz ( alto sax ) , Zoot Sims ( tenor sax , alto sax ) , Al Cohn ( tenor sax , baritone sax ) , Freddie Green ( guitar ) , Henry Grimes ( bass ) , Dave Bailey ( drums )", "traversal_to": "table:Allen Eager:row:9", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:147", "head": "table:Allen Eager:row:9", "relation": "title", "tail": "table:Allen Eager:row:9:cell:Title", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Allen Eager", "row_index": 9, "column_name": "Title", "header_path": ["Title"], "structural": true, "cell_node": true, "cell_value": "The Gerry Mulligan Songbook", "traversal_from": "table:Allen Eager:row:9", "traversal_to": "table:Allen Eager:row:9:cell:Title", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "With Lee Konitz ( 