(initial letter K):row:0", "traversal_to": "Honolulu , Hawaii", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:341", "head": "Honolulu , Hawaii", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Honolulu", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K)", "row_index": 0, "column_name": "City and state", "header_path": ["City and state"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Honolulu", "text": "Honolulu ( /ˌhɒnəˈluːluː/ ; Hawaiian : [ honoˈlulu ] ) is the capital and largest city of the U.S. state of Hawaii . It is an unincorporated part of and the county seat of the City and County of Honolulu along the southeast coast of the island of Oʻahu . [ a ] The city is the main gateway to Hawaiʻi and a major portal into the United States . The city is also a major hub for international business and military defense , as well as being host to a diverse variety of east-west and Pacific cultures , cuisine , and traditions . Honolulu is the remotest city of its size in the world , and is the westernmost and southernmost major U.S. city . For statistical purposes , the United States Census Bureau recognizes the approximate area commonly referred to as City of Honolulu ( not to be confused with the City and County ) as a census county division ( CCD ) . Honolulu is a major financial center of the islands and of the Pacific Ocean . The population of the Honolulu census designated place ( CDP ) was 359,870 as of the 2017 population estimate , while the Honolulu CCD was 390,738 and the population of the consolidated city and county was 953,207 . Honolulu means sheltered harbor or calm port in Hawaiian . The old name is Kou , a district roughly encompassing the area from Nuʻuanu Avenue to Alakea Street and from Hotel Street to Queen Street which is the heart of the present downtown district . The city has been the capital of the Hawaiian Islands since 1845 and gained historical recognition following the attack on Pearl Harbor by Japan near the city on December 7 , 1941 . As of 2015 [ update ] , Honolulu was ranked high on world livability rankings , and was also ranked as the 2nd safest city in the U.S .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "Honolulu , Hawaii", "traversal_to": "passage:/wiki/Honolulu", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "KAAH-TV --has_record--> table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:0", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:0 --city_and_state--> Honolulu , Hawaii", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "Honolulu , Hawaii --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Honolulu", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.5714, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 11.6167}}, {"path_id": "row_18_106", "score": 8.0167, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 0.5, "relation_match": 0.6667, "text_context_match": 0.25, "query_coverage": 0.8, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constraint_coverage": 0.0, "cross_modal_completeness": 1.5, "row_context": 1.0, "row_entity_binding": 1.0, "numeric_literal_coverage": 0.0, "strong_keyword_coverage": 0.0, "hyperlink_passage_bridge": 2.0, "table_witness_match": 0.0, "answer_type_path_filter": 0.0, "same_fact_corroboration": 0.0, "length_penalty": 0.7}, "nodes": ["KALB-TV", "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:18", "Alexandria , Louisiana", "passage:/wiki/Alexandria,_Louisiana"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:301", "head": "KALB-TV", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:18", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K)", "row_index": 18, "column_name": "Call letters", "header_path": ["Call letters"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "KALB-TV", "traversal_to": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:18", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:314", "head": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:18", "relation": "city_and_state", "tail": "Alexandria , Louisiana", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K)", "row_index": 18, "column_name": "City and state", "header_path": ["City and state"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:18", "traversal_to": "Alexandria , Louisiana", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:432", "head": "Alexandria , Louisiana", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Alexandria,_Louisiana", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K)", "row_index": 18, "column_name": "City and state", "header_path": ["City and state"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Alexandria,_Louisiana", "text": "Alexandria is the ninth-largest city in the state of Louisiana and is the parish seat of Rapides Parish , Louisiana , United States . It lies on the south bank of the Red River in almost the exact geographic center of the state . It is the principal city of the Alexandria metropolitan area ( population 153,922 ) which encompasses all of Rapides and Grant parishes . Its neighboring city is Pineville . In 2010 , the population was 47,723 , an increase of 3 percent from the 2000 census .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "Alexandria , Louisiana", "traversal_to": "passage:/wiki/Alexandria,_Louisiana", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "KALB-TV --has_record--> table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:18", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:18 --city_and_state--> Alexandria , Louisiana", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "Alexandria , Louisiana --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Alexandria,_Louisiana", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.5714, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 11.6167}}, {"path_id": "row_12_74", "score": 7.7667, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 0.0, "relation_match": 0.6667, "text_context_match": 0.5, "query_coverage": 0.8, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constraint_coverage": 0.0, "cross_modal_completeness": 1.5, "row_context": 1.0, "row_entity_binding": 1.0, "numeric_literal_coverage": 0.0, "strong_keyword_coverage": 0.0, "hyperlink_passage_bridge": 2.0, "table_witness_match": 0.0, "answer_type_path_filter": 0.0, "same_fact_corroboration": 0.0, "length_penalty": 0.7}, "nodes": ["KAIL", "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:12", "Fresno , California", "passage:/wiki/Fresno,_California"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:205", "head": "KAIL", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:12", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K)", "row_index": 12, "column_name": "Call letters", "header_path": ["Call letters"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "KAIL", "traversal_to": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:12", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:218", "head": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:12", "relation": "city_and_state", "tail": "Fresno , California", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K)", "row_index": 12, "column_name": "City and state", "header_path": ["City and state"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:12", "traversal_to": "Fresno , California", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:406", "head": "Fresno , California", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Fresno,_California", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K)", "row_index": 12, "column_name": "City and state", "header_path": ["City and state"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Fresno,_California", "text": "Fresno ( /ˈfrɛznoʊ/ FREZ-noh ; Spanish for ash tree ) is a city in and the county seat of Fresno County , California , United States . It covers about 112 square miles ( 290 km2 ) in the center of the San Joaquin Valley , the southern portion of California 's Central Valley . Named for the abundant ash trees lining the San Joaquin River , Fresno was founded in 1872 as a railway station of the Central Pacific Railroad before it was incorporated in 1885 . The city has since become an economic hub of Fresno County and the San Joaquin Valley , with much of the surrounding areas in the Metropolitan Fresno region predominantly tied to large-scale agricultural production . The population of Fresno grew from 134,000 in 1960 to 428,000 in 2000 . With a census-estimated 2018 population of 530,093 , Fresno is the fifth-most populous city in California , the most populous inland city in California , and the 34th-most populous city in the nation . Fresno is near the geographical center of California . It lies approximately 220 miles ( 350 km ) north of Los Angeles , 170 miles ( 270 km ) south of the state capital , Sacramento , and 185 miles ( 300 km ) southeast of San Francisco . Yosemite National Park is about 60 miles ( 100 km ) to the north , Kings Canyon National Park is 60 miles ( 100 km ) to the east , and Sequoia National Park is 75 miles ( 120 km ) to the southeast .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "Fresno , California", "traversal_to": "passage:/wiki/Fresno,_California", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "KAIL --has_record--> table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:12", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:12 --city_and_state--> Fresno , California", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "Fresno , California --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Fresno,_California", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.5714, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 11.3667}}, {"path_id": "row_8_52", "score": 7.7667, "score_components": {"grounded_edges": 1.0, "query_entity_match": 0.0, "relation_match": 0.6667, "text_context_match": 0.5, "query_coverage": 0.8, "single_venue_specificity": 0.0, "constraint_coverage": 0.0, "cross_modal_completeness": 1.5, "row_context": 1.0, "row_entity_binding": 1.0, "numeric_literal_coverage": 0.0, "strong_keyword_coverage": 0.0, "hyperlink_passage_bridge": 2.0, "table_witness_match": 0.0, "answer_type_path_filter": 0.0, "same_fact_corroboration": 0.0, "length_penalty": 0.7}, "nodes": ["KAET", "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:8", "Phoenix , Arizona", "passage:/wiki/Phoenix,_Arizona"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:139", "head": "KAET", "relation": "has_record", "tail": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:8", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K)", "row_index": 8, "column_name": "Call letters", "header_path": ["Call letters"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "KAET", "traversal_to": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:8", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:151", "head": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:8", "relation": "city_and_state", "tail": "Phoenix , Arizona", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K)", "row_index": 8, "column_name": "City and state", "header_path": ["City and state"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:8", "traversal_to": "Phoenix , Arizona", "direction": "forward"}, {"edge_id": "record:388", "head": "Phoenix , Arizona", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Phoenix,_Arizona", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K)", "row_index": 8, "column_name": "City and state", "header_path": ["City and state"], "structural": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Phoenix,_Arizona", "text": "Phoenix is the capital and most populous city in Arizona , with 1,660,272 people ( as of 2018 [ update ] ) . It is also the fifth most populous city in the United States , and the only state capital with a population of more than one million residents . Phoenix is the anchor of the Phoenix metropolitan area , also known as the Valley of the Sun , which in turn is part of the Salt River Valley . The metropolitan area is the 11th largest by population in the United States , with approximately 4.73 million people as of 2017 [ update ] . Phoenix is the seat of Maricopa County and the largest city in the state at 517.9 square miles ( 1,341 km2 ) , more than twice the size of Tucson and one of the largest cities in the United States . Phoenix was settled in 1867 as an agricultural community near the confluence of the Salt and Gila Rivers and was incorporated as a city in 1881 . It became the capital of Arizona Territory in 1889 . It is in the northeastern reaches of the Sonoran Desert and has a hot desert climate . Despite this , its canal system led to a thriving farming community with the original settler 's crops remaining important parts of the Phoenix economy for decades , such as alfalfa , cotton , citrus , and hay . Cotton , cattle , citrus , climate , and copper were known locally as the Five C 's anchoring Phoenix 's economy . These remained the driving forces of the city until after World War II , when high-tech companies began to move into the valley and air conditioning made Phoenix 's hot summers more bearable . The city averaged a four percent annual population growth rate over a 40-year period from the mid-1960s to the mid-2000s .", "context_before": ""}], "traversal_from": "Phoenix , Arizona", "traversal_to": "passage:/wiki/Phoenix,_Arizona", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "KAET --has_record--> table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:8", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "table:List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K):row:8 --city_and_state--> Phoenix , Arizona", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "Phoenix , Arizona --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Phoenix,_Arizona", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.5714, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 11.3667}}, {"path_id": "answer_evidence_semantic_100_0", "score": 82.0, "score_components": {"reverse_answer_match": 82.0}, "nodes": ["Wailuku , Hawaii", "/wiki/Wailuku,_Hawaii"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "semantic:100:0", "head": "Wailuku , Hawaii", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "/wiki/Wailuku,_Hawaii", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List of television stations in the United States by call sign (initial letter K)", "source_group": null, "row_index": 11, "column_name": "City and state", "header_path": ["City and state"], "structural": false, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Wailuku,_Hawaii", "text": "Wailuku is a census-designated place ( CDP ) in and county seat of Maui County , Hawaii , United States . The population was 15,313 at the 2010 census . Wailuku is located just west of Kahului , at the mouth of the Iao Valley . In the early 20th century Wailuku was the main tourist destination on Maui , though it has since been eclipsed with the rise of the resort towns such as Kaanapali , so much so that there are currently no hotels to speak of in Wailuku . Historic sites in the town include Kaʻahumanu Church ( named after one of Hawaiʻi 's great monarchs , Queen Kaʻahumanu ) which dates to 1876 , the Wailuku Civic Center Historic District , the site of the Chee Kung Tong Society Building , and the Bailey House , a 19th-century former seminary and home that houses a history museum and the Maui Historical Society . There are two ancient temples near Wailuku , called heiau - the Halekiʻi Heiau and the Pihanakalani Heiau . Both date back hundreds of years and were used for religious purposes by the native Hawaiians . [ citation needed ] Wailuku is served by Kahului Airport .", "context_before": ""}]}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Wailuku , Hawaii --linked_passage--> /wiki/Wailuku,_Hawaii", "depends_on": null}], "path_verification": {"status": "answer_evidence", "selection_score": 82.0, "hard_failures": []}, "created_after_answer": true}], "best_path_id": "grounded_143", "best_path_score": 9.3167, "execution_mode": "path_text", "code_generated": false, "program_executed": false, "text_extraction_mode": "direct_context_no_llm", "path_context_policy": "planner_top_n_paths_only", "top_n_paths": 5, "llm_calls": 1, "llm_api_attempts": 1, "llm_successful_calls": 1, "llm_failed_calls": 0, "llm_prompt_chars": 15529, "llm_response_chars": 10, "llm_latency_ms": 3179.79, "wall_time_ms": 21244.9, "non_llm_time_ms": 18065.11, "input_tokens": null, "output_tokens": null, "exact_match": 0.0, "semantic_exact_match": 0.0, "f1": 0.6666666666666666, "execution_exact_match": null, "retrieval_audit": {"gold_row_recall": 1.0, "gold_hyperlink_recall": 1.0, "gold_passage_recall": 0.0}, "error_category": "retrieval_miss", "is_ambiguous": null, "ambiguity_status": null}
