 According to the township web page , Moscow was first called Little Kalamazoo , and that the name Moscow was chosen by drawing the name out of a hat . Moscow Township was established in 1835 .", "context_before": "Somerset Township is a civil township of Hillsdale County in the U.S. state of Michigan . The population was 4,277 at the 2000 census . The Grand River , Michigan 's longest river , begins at natural springs within the township . The W. H. L. McCourtie Estate , originally called Aiden Lair and now known as McCourtie Park , is a recreational park located at 10426 South Jackson Road ( at US 12 ) in Somerset Center , Michigan . It was designated a Michigan State Historic Site in 1991 and listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1992 . The site may contain the country 's largest collection of el trabejo rustico ( known in French as faux bois ) , the Mexican folk art tradition where wet concrete is sculpted to look like wood ."}], "traversal_from": "Moscow", "traversal_to": "passage:/wiki/Moscow,_Michigan", "direction": "forward"}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Michigan and Ohio Railroad Moscow Depot --location--> 7324 Chicago Road [traverse reverse]", "depends_on": null}, {"step": 2, "goal": "Michigan and Ohio Railroad Moscow Depot --city--> Moscow", "depends_on": 1}, {"step": 3, "goal": "Moscow --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Moscow,_Michigan", "depends_on": 2}], "path_verification": {"status": "qualified", "hard_failures": [], "question_term_coverage": 0.8, "table_witness_indices": [], "linked_witness": false, "numeric_evidence": null, "terminal_is_container": true, "selection_score": 11.3}}, {"path_id": "answer_evidence_record_309", "score": 103.0, "score_components": {"reverse_answer_match": 103.0}, "nodes": ["Moscow, Michigan", "passage:/wiki/Moscow,_Michigan"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:309", "head": "Moscow, Michigan", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Moscow,_Michigan", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "List