ione Sportiva Dilettantistica Pro Recco ) is an Italian water polo club from Recco , in Liguria . It currently plays in Serie A1 .", "context_before": "Recco ( Latin : Ricina / Recina ) is a comune in the Metropolitan City of Genoa , region of Liguria , Italy . It is known for its focaccia al formaggio ( focaccia with cheese ) which is made with stracchino . The consortium that dictates the official recipe of the focaccia , supposedly the result of a Saracen attack in the 13th century , has obtained the European Union PGI status for the recipe . Recco is home to the September 8 fireworks festival honoring the Virgin Mary . The town is also known for its successful waterpolo team , Pro Recco . During World War II Recco 's railway was bombed by the Allies , destroying the town . It was rebuilt in the late forties and early 1950s ."}], "traversal_from": "/wiki/Pro_Recco", "traversal_to": "Pro Recco ( 8 )", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:12", "head": "table:European Cup, Euroleague and LEN Champions League records and statistics:row:0", "relation": "winning_clubs", "tail": "Pro Recco ( 8 )", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "European Cup, Euroleague and LEN Champions League records and statistics", "row_index": 0, "column_name": "Winning clubs", "header_path": ["Winning clubs"], "structural": true, "traversal_from": "Pro Recco ( 8 )", "traversal_to": "table:European Cup, Euroleague and LEN Champions League records and statistics:row:0", "direction": "reverse"}, {"edge_id": "record:6", "head": "table:European Cup, Euroleague and LEN Champions League records and statistics:row:0", "relation": "runners_up", "tail": "table:European Cup, Euroleague and LEN Champions League records and statistics:row:0:cell:Runners-up", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "European Cup, Euroleague and LEN Champions League records and statistics", "row_index": 0, "column_name": "Runners-up", "header_path": ["Runners-up"], "structural": true, "cell_node": true, "cell_value": 