{"id": "03c009db09f4dc99", "question": "What is the location of the church that has a mural by the artist Hans Feibusch from Germany ?", "gold_answer": "Goring-by-Sea", "answer": "Goring-by-Sea, Worthing, West Sussex, England", "method": "path_text_top_n", "provider": "openai_compatible", "model": "GPT-OSS-120B", "temperature": 0.0, "latency_ms": 23458.07, "prompt_chars": 11804, "synthesis_prompt_chars": 11804, "grounding_prompt_chars": 0, "synthesis_retry_attempted": false, "raw_synthesis_response": "Goring-by-Sea, Worthing, West Sussex, England", "request_max_output_tokens": 1024, "answer_retry_attempted": false, "answer_fallback_used": false, "retry_prompt_chars": 0, "raw_final_judge_response": null, "retry_raw_final_judge_response": null, "llm_selected_path_ids": [], "llm_selected_path_id": null, "final_judge_evidence_edge_ids": [], "final_judge_response_format": "deterministic_reverse_grounding", "final_judge_valid": false, "final_judge_failure_reason": "answer_match_below_grounding_threshold", "grounding_audit": {"status": "ungrounded", "reason": "answer_match_below_grounding_threshold", "best_score": 3.0}, "kg_summary": {"num_nodes": 203, "num_edges": 279, "num_record_edges": 635, "num_text_contexts": 8, "num_contextualized_nodes": 20, "num_contextualized_edges": 24, "relations": ["denomination_affiliation", "full_name", "grade", "linked_passage", "located_in", "location", "notes"], "num_rule_text_edges": 0, "num_entity_aliases": 1, "entity_resolution": {"lexical": 1}, "num_rejected_triples": 0, "num_extraction_errors": 0, "node_types": {"St Mary 's Church": ["Entity"], "Broadwater 50°49′40″N 0°22′24″W / 50.8278°N 0.3733°W / 50.8278 ; -0.3733 ( St Mary 's Church , Broadwater )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Anglican": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "I": ["Attribute"], "Broadwater 's parish church has Saxon origins , but the present structure is late Norman . Nairn and Pevsner noted that the cruciform building , of flint with stone dressings , has impressive arches . The chancel was extensively remodelled in the 19th century": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Goring-by-Sea 50°48′47″N 0°25′29″W / 50.8130°N 0.4246°W / 50.8130 ; -0.4246 ( St Mary 's Church , Goring-by-Sea )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "II*": ["Attribute"], "Decimus Burton rebuilt this late Norman church in the Gothic style in 1837 . Hans Feibusch 's mural representing Christ in Majesty , designed in 1954 , is above the chancel arch . The exterior is rendered": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "St Andrew 's Church": ["Entity"], "West Tarring 50°49′29″N 0°23′45″W / 50.8247°N 0.3958°W / 50.8247 ; -0.3958 ( St Andrew 's Church , West Tarring )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "West Tarring 's partly 13th-century parish church , in the Early English style , has Italian mosaic designs by William Butterfield in 1885 , when a major restoration took place . Its longstanding ecclesiastical status as a peculier of Canterbury Cathedral may have influenced its design": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Christ Church": ["Entity"], "Worthing 50°48′48″N 0°22′25″W / 50.8132°N 0.3737°W / 50.8132 ; -0.3737 ( Christ Church , Worthing )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Worthing 's second Anglican church , built in 1840-1843 as a chapel of ease to Broadwater and parished in 1855 , was reprieved from closure in 2006 . The flint building also uses artificial stone - an early example of this . The chancel was altered in 1894 , when a hammerbeam roof - likened to Bryant and May matchsticks by Harry Stuart Goodhart-Rendel - was added": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "St Symphorian 's Church": ["Entity"], "Durrington 50°50′11″N 0°24′48″W / 50.8364°N 0.4133°W / 50.8364 ; -0.4133 ( St Symphorian 's Church , Durrington )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "The ancient parish church was wrecked during the English Civil War , and remained disused until Lacy W. Ridge built a new structure incorporating its remains . It opened in 1916 and was extended ( with a chancel ) in 1941": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "St George 's Church": ["Entity"], "East Worthing 50°48′51″N 0°21′26″W / 50.8142°N 0.3573°W / 50.8142 ; -0.3573 ( St George 's Church , East Worthing )": ["Attribute"], "George Truefitt 's Bargate stone , Decorated Gothic-style church was consecrated in 1868 and extended in 1875 and 1884 . The chancel and adjacent aisle have large apses , and there is a bell-tower with a spirelet . The interior was refitted in 1990-91": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "St Botolph 's Church": ["Entity"], "Heene 50°48′49″N 0°23′12″W / 50.8136°N 0.3867°W / 50.8136 ; -0.3867 ( St Botolph 's Church , Heene )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "The ancient chapel at Heene , was ruined by the 18th century and partly dismantled in 1766 . A fragment remains near the present church flint and stone church , built in the Early English style in 1873 by Edmund Scott and enlarged in 1905": ["Attribute"], "St John the Divine Church": ["Entity"], "West Worthing 50°48′53″N 0°24′01″W / 50.8147°N 0.4004°W / 50.8147 ; -0.4004 ( St John the Divine Church , West Worthing )": ["Attribute"], "In 1937 , N.F . Cachemaille-Day built a brick and flint church to replace a mission chapel linked to St Botolph 's . This building of 1900 was incorporated into the new structure , which was extended in 1965 when the short , broad tower and spire were added": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Holy Trinity Church": ["Entity"], "Worthing 50°48′41″N 0°22′43″W / 50.8113°N 0.3786°W / 50.8113 ; -0.3786 ( Holy Trinity Church , Worthing )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Late 19th-century housing development in the Gratwicke area west of the town centre resulted in the building of this church in 1882-1883 . It was parished almost immediately . Henry Coe and S. Robinson 's Early English design , in dark red brick , lacked the present tower ; this was added in 1888": ["Attribute"], "Worthing 50°48′55″N 0°22′39″W / 50.8153°N 0.3774°W / 50.8153 ; -0.3774 ( St Andrew 's Church , Worthing )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Worthing 's first High Church Anglican church was so controversial that it stood unused for six years while liturgical differences were thrashed out . Arthur Blomfield 's Early English church , eventually consecrated in 1888 , uses flint and stonework extensively": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Queen Street Church Centre": ["Entity"], "Broadwater 50°49′26″N 0°22′34″W / 50.8240°N 0.3760°W / 50.8240 ; -0.3760 ( Queen Street Church Centre , Broadwater )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "-": ["Attribute"], "This combined church and community centre was built in 1993-1994 on the site of the former Broadwater Mission Hall , administered from St Mary 's Church . The present church is part of St Mary 's parish": ["Attribute"], "St Stephen 's Church": ["Entity"], "East Worthing 50°49′23″N 0°21′37″W / 50.8231°N 0.3604°W / 50.8231 ; -0.3604 ( St Stephen 's Church , East Worthing )": ["Attribute"], "Between 1929 and 1959 , this was a mission chapel to St Mary 's Church in Broadwater ; but it was consecrated in 1959 and became a separate church in its own right . It remains within the parish of St Mary 's": ["Attribute"], "All Saints Church": ["Entity"], "Findon Valley 50°51′01″N 0°23′45″W / 50.8504°N 0.3959°W / 50.8504 ; -0.3959 ( All Saints Church , Findon Valley )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "A church hall , erected in 1936 , was used for services in this interwar housing estate until Keir Hett 's brick church of 1956 was consecrated on 22 February of that year . The congregation chose the dedication . The church was parished in 1989 , and St Peter 's Church at High Salvington was added to the parish in 2010": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "St Laurence 's Church": ["Entity"], "Goring-by-Sea 50°48′32″N 0°24′27″W / 50.8090°N 0.4074°W / 50.8090 ; -0.4074 ( St Laurence 's Church , Goring-by-Sea )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Part of the parish of Goring-by-Sea , this church was founded in 1936 . An attached hall was added in 1962 . The interior has a 15th-century altarpiece retrieved from St Mary 's Church , Slaugham": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "St Peter 's Church": ["Entity"], "High Salvington 50°50′55″N 0°24′29″W / 50.8485°N 0.4081°W / 50.8485 ; -0.4081 ( St Peter 's Church , High Salvington )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "The vicar of St Symphorian 's Church paid for a tin tabernacle to be erected in High Salvington in 1928 . It was part of St Symphorian 's parish between 1951 and 2010 - since when it has been linked to All Saints Church at Findon Valley - and is Worthing 's only iron church": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "St Richard 's Church": ["Entity"], "Maybridge 50°49′16″N 0°25′06″W / 50.8210°N 0.4183°W / 50.8210 ; -0.4183 ( St Richard 's Church , Maybridge )": ["Attribute"], "This postwar housing estate north of Goring-by-Sea received a permanent church in 1966 , when Romilly Craze 's brick building opened . A church hall had accommodated services since 1954 . A parish was created in 1980": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "St Matthew 's Church": ["Entity"], "Worthing 50°49′04″N 0°22′59″W / 50.8179°N 0.3830°W / 50.8179 ; -0.3830 ( St Matthew 's Church , Worthing )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "R.S . Hyde 's Early English-style church has an apse and a narrow flèche , and uses locally quarried flint . It was built in 1899 and extended with vestries and aisles in 1911": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Broadwater Baptist Church": ["Entity"], "Broadwater 50°49′37″N 0°21′53″W / 50.8270°N 0.3648°W / 50.8270 ; -0.3648 ( Broadwater Baptist Church )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "Baptist": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "R.W . Brough 's 1968 brick structure is the successor to a church hall used since 1937 by Broadwater 's Baptist community , which had first met in 1881 in a former stable . Another building on a different site was also used between 1904 and 1937": ["Attribute"], "New Life Baptist Church": ["Entity"], "Durrington 50°50′07″N 0°24′26″W / 50.8354°N 0.4073°W / 50.8354 ; -0.4073 ( New Life Baptist Church , Durrington )": ["Attribute", "Entity"], "This church acquired its name in 1985 but has its origins in a Free Church of 1912 which became Baptist in 1943 . The present brick building , replacing the earlier structure , was completed in 1939": ["Attribute"], "East Worthing Baptist Church": ["Entity"], "East Worthing 50°48′56″N 0°21′09″W / 50.8156°N 0.3525°W / 50.8156 ; -0.3525 ( East Worthing Baptist Church )": ["Attribute"], "In 1933 , an Evangelical community founded a church in East Worthing ; it was opened by Worthing 's mayor the following year . The Baptist Church acquired the building , a brick structure designed by T.R . Hyde , in 1946": ["Attribute"], "/wiki/St_Mary's_Church,_Broadwater": ["Attribute"], "St Mary's Church, Broadwater": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Broadwater,_West_Sussex": ["Attribute"], "Broadwater 50°49′40″N 0°22′24″W": ["Entity"], "50.8278°N 0.3733°W": ["Entity"], "-0.3733 ( St Mary 's Church , Broadwater )": ["Entity"], "Broadwater, West Sussex": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Church_of_England": ["Attribute"], "Church of England": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Norman_architecture": ["Attribute"], "Norman architecture": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Ian_Nairn": ["Attribute"], "Ian Nairn": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Nikolaus_Pevsner": ["Attribute"], "Nikolaus Pevsner": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Flint": ["Attribute"], "Flint": ["Entity"], "/wiki/St_Mary's_Church,_Goring-by-Sea": ["Attribute"], "St Mary's Church, Goring-by-Sea": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Goring-by-Sea": ["Attribute"], "Goring-by-Sea 50°48′47″N 0°25′29″W": ["Entity"], "50.8130°N 0.4246°W": ["Entity"], "-0.4246 ( St Mary 's Church , Goring-by-Sea )": ["Entity"], "Goring-by-Sea": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Decimus_Burton": ["Attribute"], "Decimus Burton": ["Entity"], "/wiki/English_Gothic_architecture": ["Attribute"], "English Gothic architecture": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Hans_Feibusch": ["Attribute"], "Hans Feibusch": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Christ_in_Majesty": ["Attribute"], "Christ in Majesty": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Stucco": ["Attribute"], "Stucco": ["Entity"], "/wiki/St_Andrew's_Church,_West_Tarring": ["Attribute"], "St Andrew's Church, West Tarring": ["Entity"], "/wiki/Tarring,_West_Sussex": ["Attribute"], "West 