.4111}}, {"path_id": "answer_evidence_record_968", "score": 283.0, "score_components": {"reverse_answer_match": 283.0}, "nodes": ["Two Pictures , BB . 59 ( Isaac Stern , Violinist Mendelssohn : Violin Concerto in E Minor , Op . 64 Tchaikovsky : Violin Concerto in D Major , Op . 35 Shostakovich Symphony No . 1 in F Minor , Op . 10", "passage:/wiki/Mstislav_Rostropovich"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:968", "head": "Two Pictures , BB . 59 ( Isaac Stern , Violinist Mendelssohn : Violin Concerto in E Minor , Op . 64 Tchaikovsky : Violin Concerto in D Major , Op . 35 Shostakovich Symphony No . 1 in F Minor , Op . 10", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Mstislav_Rostropovich", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Original Jacket Collection", "row_index": 13, "column_name": "Set Details", "header_path": ["Set Details"], "structural": true, "derived_from_cell_split": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Mstislav_Rostropovich", "text": "Mstislav Leopoldovich Slava Rostropovich ( Russian : Мстисла́в Леопо́льдович Ростропо́вич , romanized : Mstislav Leopol'dovič Rostropovič , pronounced [ rəstrɐˈpovʲɪtɕ ] ; 27 March 1927 - 27 April 2007 ) was a Soviet and Russian cellist and conductor . He is considered to be one of the greatest cellists of the 20th century . In addition to his interpretations and technique , he was well known for both inspiring and commissioning new works , which enlarged the cello repertoire more than any cellist before or since . He inspired and premiered over 100 pieces , forming long-standing friendships and artistic partnerships with composers including Dmitri Shostakovich , Sergei Prokofiev , Henri Dutilleux , Witold Lutosławski , Olivier Messiaen , Luciano Berio , Krzysztof Penderecki , Alfred Schnittke , Norbert Moret , Andreas Makris , Leonard Bernstein , Aram Khachaturian and Benjamin Britten . Rostropovich was internationally recognized as a staunch advocate of human rights , and was awarded the 1974 Award of the International League of Human Rights . He was married to the soprano Galina Vishnevskaya and had two daughters , Olga and Elena Rostropovich .", "context_before": ""}]}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Two Pictures , BB . 59 ( Isaac Stern , Violinist Mendelssohn : Violin Concerto in E Minor , Op . 64 Tchaikovsky : Violin Concerto in D Major , Op . 35 Shostakovich Symphony No . 1 in F Minor , Op . 10 --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Mstislav_Rostropovich", "depends_on": null}], "path_verification": {"status": "answer_evidence", "selection_score": 283.0, "hard_failures": []}, "created_after_answer": true}, {"path_id": "answer_evidence_record_998", "score": 283.0, "score_components": {"reverse_answer_match": 283.0}, "nodes": ["Two Pictures , BB . 59 ( Isaac Stern , Violinist Mendelssohn : Violin Concerto in E Minor , Op . 64 Tchaikovsky : Violin Concerto in D Major , Op . 35 Shostakovich Symphony No . 1 in F Minor , Op . 10", "passage:/wiki/Bist_du_bei_mir"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "record:998", "head": "Two Pictures , BB . 59 ( Isaac Stern , Violinist Mendelssohn : Violin Concerto in E Minor , Op . 64 Tchaikovsky : Violin Concerto in D Major , Op . 35 Shostakovich Symphony No . 1 in F Minor , Op . 10", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "passage:/wiki/Bist_du_bei_mir", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Original Jacket Collection", "row_index": 13, "column_name": "Set Details", "header_path": ["Set Details"], "structural": true, "derived_from_cell_split": true, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Bist_du_bei_mir", "text": "Bist du bei mir , geh ich mit Freuden ( If you are with me , I go with joy ) is an aria from Gottfried Heinrich Stölzel 's opera Diomedes . The aria is best known as Bist du bei mir , BWV 508 , a version for voice and continuo found as No . 25 in the 1725 Notebook for Anna Magdalena Bach .", "context_before": "Isaac Stern ( July 21 , 1920 - September 22 , 2001 ) was an American violinist . Mstislav Leopoldovich Slava Rostropovich ( Russian : Мстисла́в Леопо́льдович Ростропо́вич , romanized : Mstislav Leopol'dovič Rostropovič , pronounced [ rəstrɐˈpovʲɪtɕ ] ; 27 March 1927 - 27 April 2007 ) was a Soviet and Russian cellist and conductor . He is considered to be one of the greatest cellists of the 20th century . In addition to his interpretations and technique , he was well known for both inspiring and commissioning new works , which enlarged the cello repertoire more than any cellist before or since . He inspired and premiered over 100 pieces , forming long-standing friendships and artistic partnerships with composers including Dmitri Shostakovich , Sergei Prokofiev , Henri Dutilleux , Witold Lutosławski , Olivier Messiaen , Luciano Berio , Krzysztof Penderecki , Alfred Schnittke , Norbert Moret , Andreas Makris , Leonard Bernstein , Aram Khachaturian and Benjamin Britten . Rostropovich was internationally recognized as a staunch advocate of human rights , and was awarded the 1974 Award of the International League of Human Rights . He was married to the soprano Galina Vishnevskaya and had two daughters , Olga and Elena Rostropovich ."}]}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Two Pictures , BB . 59 ( Isaac Stern , Violinist Mendelssohn : Violin Concerto in E Minor , Op . 64 Tchaikovsky : Violin Concerto in D Major , Op . 35 Shostakovich Symphony No . 1 in F Minor , Op . 10 --linked_passage--> passage:/wiki/Bist_du_bei_mir", "depends_on": null}], "path_verification": {"status": "answer_evidence", "selection_score": 283.0, "hard_failures": []}, "created_after_answer": true}, {"path_id": "answer_evidence_semantic_628_0", "score": 283.0, "score_components": {"reverse_answer_match": 283.0}, "nodes": ["Two Pictures , BB . 59 ( Isaac Stern , Violinist Mendelssohn : Violin Concerto in E Minor , Op . 64 Tchaikovsky : Violin Concerto in D Major , Op . 35 Shostakovich Symphony No . 1 in F Minor , Op . 10", "/wiki/Mstislav_Rostropovich"], "edges": [{"edge_id": "semantic:628:0", "head": "Two Pictures , BB . 59 ( Isaac Stern , Violinist Mendelssohn : Violin Concerto in E Minor , Op . 64 Tchaikovsky : Violin Concerto in D Major , Op . 35 Shostakovich Symphony No . 1 in F Minor , Op . 10", "relation": "linked_passage", "tail": "/wiki/Mstislav_Rostropovich", "source_type": "table", "source_id": "Original Jacket Collection", "source_group": null, "row_index": 13, "column_name": "Set Details", "header_path": ["Set Details"], "structural": false, "contexts": [{"source_id": "/wiki/Mstislav_Rostropovich", "text": "Mstislav Leopoldovich Slava Rostropovich ( Russian : Мстисла́в Леопо́льдович Ростропо́вич , romanized : Mstislav Leopol'dovič Rostropovič , pronounced [ rəstrɐˈpovʲɪtɕ ] ; 27 March 1927 - 27 April 2007 ) was a Soviet and Russian cellist and conductor . He is considered to be one of the greatest cellists of the 20th century . In addition to his interpretations and technique , he was well known for both inspiring and commissioning new works , which enlarged the cello repertoire more than any cellist before or since . He inspired and premiered over 100 pieces , forming long-standing friendships and artistic partnerships with composers including Dmitri Shostakovich , Sergei Prokofiev , Henri Dutilleux , Witold Lutosławski , Olivier Messiaen , Luciano Berio , Krzysztof Penderecki , Alfred Schnittke , Norbert Moret , Andreas Makris , Leonard Bernstein , Aram Khachaturian and Benjamin Britten . Rostropovich was internationally recognized as a staunch advocate of human rights , and was awarded the 1974 Award of the International League of Human Rights . He was married to the soprano Galina Vishnevskaya and had two daughters , Olga and Elena Rostropovich .", "context_before": ""}]}], "steps": [{"step": 1, "goal": "Two Pictures , BB . 59 ( Isaac Stern , Violinist Mendelssohn : Violin Concerto in E Minor , Op . 64 Tchaikovsky : Violin Concerto in D Major , Op . 35 Shostakovich Symphony No . 1 in F Minor , Op . 10 --linked_passage--> /wiki/Mstislav_Rostropovich", "depends_on": null}], "path_verification": {"s